hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"14029","(14029) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was He performs Hajj using his children. Whoever among them is able to stone the stone, and whoever is not able to stone it on his behalf."
"14030","(14030) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib Al-Muallem, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Should he throw stones of stones at him? He said: Yes."
"14031","(14031) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the boy’s ihram, he said: His father or guardian may perform the prayer on his behalf."
"14032","(14032) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brushed the animal’s hair on the right hump and shed the blood from it."
"14033","(14033) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; If he wanted to feel the body, he would make it feel on the right side."
"14034","(14034) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; If there was one body, he would feel it in its left side with his right hand, and if there were two bodies, One of them is hairy in the right side, and the other is in the left side."
"14035","(14035) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He said: It feels in the right hand."
"14036","(14036) Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He had hair on the right side."
"14037","(14037) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; He said: Make it feel wherever you want."
"14038","(14038) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There were people who came to Mecca without Supplies, so it was revealed: {And provide for yourself, for indeed the best provision is piety}"
"14039","(14039) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ata’ al-Bakai, who said: I asked al-Sha’bi about the Almighty’s saying: {And provide for yourself, for the best provision is piety}? He said: Food, and food that day will be short. I said: What is food? He said: Suwaiq and dates."
"14040","(14040) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; {And provide for yourself} He said: Al-Khashkanang and Al-Suwaiq."
"14041","(14041) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: There were people from the people of Yemen who, when they performed Hajj, did not They will provide for themselves until they reach the end of such-and-such, so it was revealed: {And provide for yourself, for indeed the best provision is piety}"
"14042","(14042) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They did not provide themselves with food during their Hajj until the following revelation was revealed: {And provide for yourself, for indeed the best provision is piety.} So provide for yourself with food."
"14043","(14043) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Omar ibn al-Khattab ordered al-Sabi ibn Ma`abad to slaughter a ram."
"14044","(14044) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The tea is sufficient for the qarin. Of this gift and sacrifice."
"14045","(14045) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: His sacrifice is sufficient for his sacrifice."
"14046","(14046) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Tawoos was asked about a woman who had sexual intercourse but did not slaughter and perform the ritual sacrifice? He said: It is sufficient."
"14047","(14047) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He used to enjoin and encourage pleasure and say: A sheep will suffice for it."
"14048","(14048) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever is caught up in war will be sacrificed from where he was detained. He is permissible for women and for all things, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did."
"14049","(14049) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; In Al-Muhshar, he said: He will be sent with his gift, so when it is slaughtered it is permissible."
"14050","(14050) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr asked me about this? So I informed him, and he said: With his hand: This is what Ibn Abbas said."
"14051","(14051) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He said in Al-Muhsir: When he returns, nothing is permissible for him except his head."
"14052","(14052) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is permissible in every way, so it is in the same position as permissible."
"14053","(14053) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: So It is permissible to sacrifice his gift."
"14054","(14054) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; A man from Wahbil was trapped, so Abdullah said: When his sacrifice is slaughtered, he is free from everything."
"14055","(14055) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In Al-Muhsir, he said: He will be sent with a gift, and when it is sacrificed, it is permissible, and he must perform Hajj from the one who came."
"14056","(14056) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He used to say: If a man made the Hajj obligatory and fulfilled it, Confinement, for he will send his gift. When the gift reaches its place, then if he wishes, he may return and be freed from some things and deprived of others. Other"
"14057","(14057) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Salim and Al-Qasim about Al-Muhssar? They said about it the words of Muhammad."
"14058","(14058) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If the Hadi of the slaughtered one is slaughtered, then everything is permissible for him. Something"
"14059","(14059) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya and Al-Aswad; They both said: Part of the completion of the Hajj is to perform the two prayers with the imam according to his custom."
"14060","(14060) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to like to pray. The two prayers; Dhuhr and Asr with the Imam at Arafat."
"14061","(14061) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He used to pray the two prayers with the imam at Arafat, the noon and the afternoon prayers."
"14062","(14062) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Safwan, on the authority of Yazid bin Shayban said: We were standing in a far place, keeping our distance from him, when Ibn Murabba’ came to us and said: I am a messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Be consistent with your feelings, for you are a legacy from the legacy of Abraham, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.

(Tirmidhi 883, Abu Dawud 1914)"
"14063","(14063) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir and Zayd ibn Aslam; They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: All of them were known to be in a position, and they rose from the belly of their den. (Ahmad 4/82, Bazzar 3443)"
"14064","(14064) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He recognized him. It's all a situation. (Abu Dawud 1932, Darmi 1879)"
"14065","(14065) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; He heard him say: He knew all of them had a position, so whoever wanted to reach the position of the Imam, and whoever wanted to write him down."
"14066","(14066) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: He knew all of them. A stop, except for the belly of 'Urna."
"14067","(14067) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, he said: Someone who saw Ibn Abbas standing at Al-Hiyad, meaning “knowledge”."
"14068","(14068) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He said: He knew all of it was a stop, except for Batn 'Urna."
"14069","(14069) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like a man to stand close. From the imam, Abdullah bin Omar said: O people, do not kill yourselves, for everything here is a situation."
"14070","(14070) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he heard Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman bin Yarubu’ tell On the authority of Jubayr bin Al-Huwaith, I heard Abu Bakr while he was standing on a straw and saying: O people, In the morning, they were in the morning, then he pushed, and it was as if I was looking at his thighs exposed by what his camel was scratching with his groin."
"14071","(14071) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubair, who said: All of Muzdalifah is a standing place, except A heartened stomach."
"14072","(14072) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He said: The plural of all of them is a position, except for the belly of the muḥsīr."
"14073","(14073) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I told him: Where was Ibn Omar standing from? Plural? He said: He would not stop losing his mind until he stopped at a rainbow."
"14074","(14074) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’: Where is he from me? He said: There is nothing between the two obstacles to a Muhassir. I do not like for anyone to descend except between the Aqaba and a Muhassir."
"14075","(14075) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Stand behind the Sacred Mash’ar. You cannot, so when you are close to it, you remember God and call upon Him, for God Almighty said: {Remember God at the Sacred Landmark}"
"14076","(14076) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer They stand in Muzdalifah, near the mountain."
"14077","(14077) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He sacrificed in Medina and shaved his head."
"14078","(14078) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I heard him say: It is not Shaving except in Mecca."
"14079","(14079) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, or Abdullah bin Abi Salama; If Ibn Umar did not perform Hajj, he would shave his head."
"14080","(14080) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham; Al-Hasan used to shave his head on the Day of Sacrifice in Basra."
"14081","(14081) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: They liked for a man to be taken from His hair on the Day of Sacrifice? He said: Yes."
"14082","(14082) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led a hundred of his body."
"14083","(14083) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Al-Ash’arī was the most venerated body."
"14084","(14084) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He has guided your body."
"14085","(14085) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Ibn al-Zubayr drove ten camels."
"14086","(14086) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to give two sacrifices during Hajj, and one sacrifice during Umrah."
"14087","(14087) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, the client of Ibn Ayyash, who said: I saw Abdullah ibn Ayash gave Mary two girls, one of which was circumcised."
"14088","(14088) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He has guided your body."
"14089","(14089) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas. Al-Azdi, on the authority of his mother, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Do not kill one another, and if If you throw stones at the Jamarat, throw them like gravel. (Abu Dawud 1961. Ahmad 5/376)"
"14090","(14090) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who narrated it, and said: Throw it like pebbles. The kidnapping

(Tirmidhi 886. Ahmad 3/301)"
"14091","(14091) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of a man from his people, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, teaching the people their rituals. He said: Then he said: Throw at the Jamarat like a gravel. (Abu Dawud 1952. Ahmad 4/61)"
"14092","(14092) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Throw the Jamarat in the same way. Kidney stones"
"14093","(14093) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: We used to collect pebbles. The kidnapping"
"14094","(14094) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ about the stones for throwing stones? He said: It was said: A pebble between two pebbles. He said: I said: What is it? He said: The pebbles with which one is thrown."
"14095","(14095) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: The pebbles with which stones are thrown. Such as gallstones."
"14096","(14096) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Al-Fadl bin Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Throw at the Jamarat like gravel.

(Muslim 268. Dharmi 1891)"
"14097","(14097) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Husayn, he said: Abu Aliyah narrated to me on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the morning after the Aqaba: He picked up pebbles for him. He said: So I picked up pebbles for him. The gravel of the gravel. He said: And he said: In the like of this, throw away: Then he said: Beware of exaggeration in religion."
"14098","(14098) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Qamtita, on the authority of Salem, who said: The written is sufficient. From the two rak'ahs of Tawaf."
"14099","(14099) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The written rite is sufficient for the two rak’ahs of tawaf."
"14100","(14100) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The obligatory prayer is sufficient for two rak’ahs. Tawaf"
"14101","(14101) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: I circumambulated the Kaaba and prepared what was written, and I wanted to pray. You prayed two rak'ahs, and then some people were sitting, so I came to a group and asked them? Then a sheikh said to me: Are you not satisfied with Ibn Omar? I saw him do it."
"14102","(14102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wabara, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; They said: The obligatory prayer is sufficient for the two rak’ahs of tawaaf."
"14103","(14103) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Sunnah has passed that there are two rak’ahs with every week, no Whether voluntary or obligatory is sufficient for them."
"14104","(14104) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: The obligatory prayer is sufficient for the two rak’ahs of tawaf."
"14105","(14105) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He hated to have any of the perfume taken from the ankle with which he could be cured, and whenever the servant saw that it was being taken He cut her off, not wanting to cause her pain.

 Ata’ said: Whenever one of us wanted to be healed with it, he would bring perfume of his own and wipe the stone with it, then take it away."
"14106","(14106) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Creatures are not removed from the House, unless it is given to them."
"14107","(14107) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I asked Mujahid and Ata’ about a person in ihram who performs ablution and the hairs fall out? They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"14108","(14108) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, who said: I heard Salim and a man ask him about a man who touched his beard and it fell. Are there any hairs? He said: Uff, ugh."
"14109","(14109) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali, and Ibn Al-Aswad; What about a man performing ablution and wiping his beard and the hairs fall out? They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"14110","(14110) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: There are no days in which God loves deeds more than these days, the ten days, so increase them in abundance. Takbeer, Tahlil, and Praise. (Ahmad 75. Bayhaqi 3475)"
"14111","(14111) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Miskin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard Mujahid, and a man said “Allahu Akbar” in days. The ten, so Mujahid said: Why did he not raise his voice, for I have overtaken them, and a man says the takbir in the mosque and the people are shaken by it. The mosque, then the sound goes out to the people of the valley until it reaches Al-Abtah, and the people of Al-Abtah shake with it, but it is its origin. From one man."
"14112","(14112) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about the takbeer on the ten days. ? They said: Hadith."
"14113","(14113) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; He used to come to Mecca and circumambulate, then he would come back and say something, so when it was evening, he would go and circumambulate between the two rows. And the marwa."
"14114","(14114) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Like him"
"14115","(14115) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm if one does Tawaf to delay the Sa’y. Until it gets cold."
"14116","(14116) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: Ishaq, a servant of Quraysh, informed me. He said: He came to us. Saeed bin Jubayr circumambulated the Kaaba seven times and prayed two rak’ahs, then delayed the Sa’y between Safa and Marwah until evening."
"14117","(14117) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to differentiate between tawaaf and sa’i."
"14118","(14118) Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It is not to be taken into account. He circumambulates the Kaaba, then circumambulates. Between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and if he does not do so until the evening, he will say: He has fulfilled his obligation, and nothing is due upon him."
"14119","(14119) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who started with al-Safa and al-Marwah before the House, he said: He is celebrating Eid."
"14120","(14120) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, who said: I saw Omar ibn Abdul Aziz in ihram, and he had to wear a haram. Ink"
"14121","(14121) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He may enter ihram for whatever he wants, if he wants two white garments. And if he wants, in two washed garments, and if he wants, in two ink garments."
"14122","(14122) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to walk in the belly of the stream, when he circumambulated between Safa and Marwa. Ibn Omar used to do that.

(Bukhari 1617, Dharmi 1841)"
"14123","(14123) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man runs between Safa and Marwa in the belly of The way is easy, and the effort is not difficult."
"14124","(14124) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: I ran with Ibn Umar in the belly of the stream."
"14125","(14125) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he wishes, he may run in the valley, and if he wishes, he may not run."
"14126","(14126) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He was sacrificing alone in the belly of the stream."
"14127","(14127) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He was running on the path."
"14128","(14128) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Al-Zubayr used to walk between Safa and Marwa in a hurry."
"14129","(14129) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: I saw them striving From the neighborhood of Banu Abbad to the alley of Banu Abi Hussein, so I said to Mujahid? He said: This is the belly of the first torrent, but the people disdained it."
"14130","(14130) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib the teacher, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who circumambulated and part of his circumambulation was entering into the Hijr, he said: The act of entering the Hijr does not count."
"14131","(14131) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of his father; He saw Salim walking around with Hisham, so Hisham wanted to enter the stone, but Salim prevented him."
"14132","(14132) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who performed the obligatory circumambulation, then passed through the stone, saying: He will repeat the circumambulation. That's why blood."
"14133","(14133) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; Omar joined the prayers of Mina."
"14134","(14134) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw people gathering with Manna and praying to Him."
"14135","(14135) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard him and he was asked about the people of Manna. He said: They are only traveling."
"14136","(14136) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Uthman, who said: I witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz not compiling Why?"
"14137","(14137) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Al-‘Aziz on the day of the Sadr and the day of the Friday prayer came, so he stayed and made the sermon on the ground before the Ka’bah, then he spoke some words, then he prayed the Friday prayer. Two rak'ahs"
"14138","(14138) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That Omar ibn al-Khattab prayed the congregational prayer with the husbah, but he did not perform it in congregation with it, but he gathered the people of the town together. Ibn Abi Dhib said: He made it. At noon"
"14139","(14139) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Zayd, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah, he said: Abdullah said: Not Ali. The Muslims will be united on their journey, and on the day we will separate them."
"14140","(14140) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, about a man cutting down trees from the Sacred Mosque. He said: In The penis is a dirham, and in the doha is a cow."
"14141","(14141) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Harith and Hammad; They said: About the one who grows from the trees of the Sanctuary. They said: It is worth its value."
"14142","(14142) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in singing, singing, and poetry. For the forbidden person unless it is obscene."
"14143","(14143) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Omar used to order a man to perform Haddad."
"14144","(14144) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Qasim, who said: I heard Al-Hasan and he was asked about the female shoe? He said: The Muslims used to do it."
"14145","(14145) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, who said: Suwayd ibn Ghaflali used to command A boy of his who will join us."
"14146","(14146) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid al-Araj, who said: I heard Muwarriq He was walking on the road to Mecca and he was saying: If they had spoken, they would have complained as an adult."
"14147","(14147) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab heard A man brought a piece of land, and he was riding with the singing of the riders. Omar said: This is from the rider’s provisions."
"14148","(14148) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met a people who were angry and angry, but when they saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he remained silent. He spoke to them and said: Who are the people? They said: From Mudar, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And I am from Mudar, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What What about your one who does not challenge? They said: O Messenger of God, we are the first Arabs to wear sandals. He said: What is that about? They said: A man from among us, and they called him his, was celibate from his camels during the days of spring, so he sent a servant of his with the camels. He said: So he delayed. The boy hit him with a stick on the hand, and the boy went off saying: What a hand, what a hand. He said: So it moved. The camels became active, he said: so he said to him: Hold on, hold on, he said: so the people opened the horseshoes. (Bayhaqi 2288 Bazar 2113)"
"14149","(14149) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not touch the stone from its right, nor To his left, but face him completely."
"14150","(14150) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, who said: He narrated to me someone who saw a mujahid turning around until he faced the The stone in front of him."
"14151","(14151) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ram in the hyena to be slaughtered in the state of Ihram. And He made him of the game. (Abu Dawud 3795. Tirmidhi 851)"
"14152","(14152) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man killed a hyena while he was in ihram, so he went to Ali. So he asked him? So he put a ram in it."
"14153","(14153) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali: Concerning the hyena when If he transgresses against a person in ihram, let him kill him, but if he kills him without transgressing against him, then it is a sinful sheep."
"14154","(14154) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Omar; Like him"
"14155","(14155) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the hyena if there is no longer a ram, and Ataa says something like that."
"14156","(14156) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Did Marwan ask him? He said: It contains a ram."
"14157","(14157) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no blood on any of the stones, except on embers. The afterlife, if he offers something before it, then he will accept it."
"14158","(14158) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who stones one Jamarat before the other one that he should start with, he said: He does not have to do anything about it."
"14159","(14159) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted remembrance."
"14160","(14160) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in the trees that have fallen. The sanctuary is to be captured."
"14161","(14161) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Al-Aswad; They said: There is no harm in the fallen trees of the Sanctuary."
"14162","(14162) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to Arafat until when the sun had risen, he ordered the retaliation to be carried out and they departed for him, so he came to the heart of the valley. So he addressed the people."
"14163","(14163) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays ibn al-Muttalib; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon with Arafah. (Tabarani 28)"
"14164","(14164) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving the sermon on the Day of Sacrifice, so the princes were busy, so they delayed it until the morning."
"14165","(14165) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Tariq, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech. May God bless him and grant him peace. On the Day of Sacrifice, people will be between the two Jamarat during the days of Tashreeq."
"14166","(14166) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj; That Omar bin Abdul Aziz delivered a sermon to them the day before the Tarwiyah, the day of sacrifice, and that Ibn al-Zubayr used to deliver the ten sermons. All of them"
"14167","(14167) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn al-Aswad, who said: I saw my father going up to Ibn Al-Zubair recognized him while he was on the pulpit. When Ibn Al-Zubair’s speech came down, I said to my father: What did you say to him? He said: I told him: I heard Omar addressing HaHana on the pulpit."
"14168","(14168) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them. Day of Sacrifice."
"14169","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abd told us Allah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba, said:

(14169) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jad’an, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not pray except two rak’ahs until he returned to Medina. I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr, and he did not pray except two rak’ahs until he returned to Medina. I performed Hajj with Omar, but he did not pray except two rak'ahs until he returned to Medina, and Uthman performed Hajj for seven years during his emirate, praying only two rak'ahs, then he prayed With Mina four."
"14170","(14170) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. peace be upon him, two rak'ahs, and Abu Bakr after him, and Omar after Abu Bakr, and Uthman emerged from his caliphate, then Uthman He then prayed four, and when Ibn Umar prayed with the imam, he would pray four, and if he prayed alone, he would pray two rak’ahs.

(Bukhari 1082, Muslim 17)"
"14171","(14171) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Harith ibn Wahhab informed me, he said: I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs in Mina as many people did."
"14172","(14172) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abu Sulaym, on the authority of Anas, said: I prayed two rak’ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Mina, with Abu Bakr, and with Omar. And with Othman he was a leader of his emirate. (Ahmad 3/144, Abu Ali 4255)"
"14173","(14173) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Awn ibn Abi Juhayf, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, perform two rak’ahs of prayers from me."
"14174","(14174) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, who said: Othman prayed. I prayed four rak'ahs in Mina, and Abdullah said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, two rak'ahs in Mina, and with Abu Bakr. Two rak'ahs, and with Omar two rak'ahs, then your paths would separate, and I wished that of the four rak'ahs I had two rak'ahs to come."
"14175","(14175) Jarir and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah. He said: A man from the people of Al-Yamamah accompanied us, and he narrated to us: He saw Ibn Umar praying two rak'ahs behind Ibn al-Zubayr in Mina. He said: And I saw him praying four rak'ahs behind al-Hajjaj."
"14176","(14176) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, Salim, and Tawus; They said: Shorten my prayers."
"14177","(14177) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Prayers at Mina are two rak’ahs, on the days of Tashreeq."
"14178","(14178) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas said, Al-Fadl ibn Abbas said: I was The buttocks of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I continued to hear him reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqabah, but when he threw it, he cut it off.

(Bukhari 1685, Muslim 266)"
"14179","(14179) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Aban bin Salih told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I paid with Hussein bin Ali from Muzdalifah, and I kept hearing him saying: “Labbaik” until he came to the Jamaraat, so I said: To him: What is this delusion, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I heard Abu Ali bin Abi Talib saying the Ihram until he reached the Jamarat, and he told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace be upon him and his family until he reached her. (Ahmad 1/114, Bazzar 500)"
"14180","(14180) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Sakhbara, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not abandon the Talbiyah until he came. Al-Aqaba unless he mixes it with takbeer or tahlil. (Ahmad 1/417, Ibn Khuzaymah 2806)"
"14181","(14181) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba, and he threw seven pebbles at it. He says “Allahu Akbar” with every pebble. (Ibn Khuzaymah 2887. Tabarani 672)"
"14182","(14182) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded. May God bless him and grant him peace until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba. (Tabarani 10990)"
"14183","(14183) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, who said: I performed Hajj with Omar for two years. One of them is in the year in which he was afflicted. All of that is fulfilled, up to and including stoning Jamarat al-Aqaba from the depths of the valley."
"14184","(14184) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That Omar recited the Talbiyah until he stoned Al-Aqabah, and that Ibn Abbas used to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat Al-Aqabah, and he said: It is only We open the solution now."
"14185","(14185) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Amer bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah; He responded until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba."
"14186","(14186) Hafs, Waki’, Marwan bin Muawiyah, and Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ata’ He said: Ali used to recite the Talbiyah, and he would stop reciting the Talbiyah when he stoned Jamarat al-Aqabah."
"14187","(14187) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, that he was not He abandons the Talbiyah until he stones Jamarat al-Aqabah."
"14188","(14188) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ikrimah; He said: Ibn Abbas sent me with Hussein bin Ali, so he responded until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba."
"14189","(14189) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: Sa`id bin al-Musayyab said: Ilal in Hajj Until you go to the position on the evening of Arafah."
"14190","(14190) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: I saw Al-Qasim interrupting the Talbiyah when he went to the station, he said: And it was Aisha does it."
"14191","(14191) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: He did not interrupt the Talbiyah during Hajj. Until he goes to Arafat."
"14192","(14192) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar used to refrain from reciting the Talbiyah. During Hajj, when he enters the Sacred Mosque, then when he circumambulates the Kaaba, he performs the prayer."
"14193","(14193) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, and Al-Aswad , on the authority of Abdullah; He would not stop reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba at the first pebble."
"14194","(14194) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: I asked Abu Ikrimah, while I was hearing about the ilāl, when Will it be cut off? So I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, insulted him until he stoned the Jamarat, and Abu Bakr and Omar."
"14195","(14195) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah; He remained steadfast until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqabah, and he cut his teeth with the first pebble."
"14196","(14196) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who narrated it; He used to refrain from reciting the Talbiyah during the Umrah when he received the stone. (Abu Dawud 1813. Tirmidhi 919)"
"14197","(14197) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hasan and Zuhayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, continued his life until he received the stone."
"14198","(14198) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed Umrah. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him for three lifetimes, and he did not stop reciting the Talbiyah until he received the stone. (Ahmad 2/180)"
"14199","(14199) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said: The pilgrim refrains from reciting the Talbiyah when he touches the stone, and the Hajj pilgrim refrains from reciting the Talbiyah when he touches the stone, and the Hajj pilgrim when he stones the Jamarat."
"14200","(14200) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Abbas used to perform the talbiyah until the age of He picks up the stone, and Ibn Omar used to cut it when he entered the Haram."
"14201","(14201) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Until he receives the stone. Ataa said: He cuts off when he enters the village."
"14202","(14202) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Mujahid; Indeed, when they were to complete Umrah, they would not refrain from reciting the Talbiyah until they received the stone."
"14203","(14203) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr bin told me Shayba, he said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz and Aban bin Othman meeting in Dhu Tawa in Al-Umrah."
"14204","(14204) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He is cut off when he enters the sanctuary."
"14205","(14205) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He cuts his hair when he sees the thrones of Mecca."
"14206","(14206) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The one performing Umrah does not break off until he has received the The stone"
"14207","(14207) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, the same."
"14208","(14208) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to stop reciting the Talbiyah during the Umrah if he entered The sanctuary"
"14209","(14209) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: Sa`id bin al-Musayyab said: Al-Ilal is in Umrah until he looks at the thrones of Mecca."
"14210","(14210) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, he said: He cuts his hair when he sees the houses of Mecca."
"14211","(14211) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Abdullah’s companions used to be confused during the Umrah. Until they receive the stone."
"14212","(14212) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is cut off in the Umrah if he receives the The stone"
"14213","(14213) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of his father, he said: I narrated with Abdullah, then he threw seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble, and he went inside the valley until when it was empty, he said: Oh God, make it An accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin. Then he said: This is how I saw the one to whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed do. (Bayhaqi 129. Ahmad 1/427)"
"14214","(14214) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Hanash, who said: I heard Ibn Umar when he stoned the stones. He says: Oh God, make him an accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin."
"14215","(14215) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no temporary supplication required to stop at the two jamarat, so say what You wish"
"14216","(14216) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan used to say: He supplicates entirely at the Jamaraat, and does not set a specific time. Something"
"14217","(14217) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Ibrahim: What should I say if I stone the Jamarat? He said: Say: Oh God, make it an accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin. He said: I said: Should I say it with every pebble? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"14218","(14218) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: I said to Ata’: Is there anything temporary in the Jamaraat that cannot be done more than that? He said: No, except the saying of Jabir."
"14219","(14219) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr and Habib bin Abi Thabit, and a man from Quraysh, after the imam had spoken on the eve of his prayers, saw him. Sa’id bin Jubayr stood up and gave the call to prayer, and the Quraysh’s mother said after that. The Imam explained."
"14220","(14220) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Sharqi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi; He prayed Maghrib without combining prayers with Omar for two years."
"14221","(14221) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He prayed without joining the mountains."
"14222","(14222) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir? He said: There is no prayer except in congregation."
"14223","(14223) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Uthman, who said: I saw Aban bin Uthman praying the Maghrib prayer in the people. Before he comes together."
"14224","(14224) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad? He said: I do not know how to pray the night in congregation unless it is in congregation."
"14225","(14225) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sakan Ibn Al-Mughirah, he said: Salem led the Maghrib prayer with us before he came. All together"
"14226","(14226) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not pray Maghrib except in congregation, unless you make a mistake. path, or your mount will go astray."
"14227","(14227) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Did you think that they prayed on the road? He said: There is no problem. I said: Have you seen if he prays the Maghrib prayer on the road, and the evening prayer in congregation? He said: No problem."
"14228","(14228) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz was standing With his knowledge, he said: O people, you have come from near and far, and you are not a single delegation, and the predecessor is not the one who His animal outpaces him, nor does his camel, and the outrunner is he whose sins God has forgiven. Then a man called him: Where should I pray Maghrib? He said: Where did you reach this valley of yours?"
"14229","(14229) Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that when he arrived from Arafat, perhaps He prayed in the left side of the mountain."
"14230","(14230) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is disliked to pray without a congregation, so if he does that it is permissible. about him"
"14231","(14231) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to dislike prayer without Muzdalifah, except for necessity."
"14232","(14232) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, he said: Usama ibn Zaid informed me, he said I departed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Arafat, and when he was some way away, I said: “Prayer,” and he said: “Prayer is in front of you.”

(Bukhari 1391, Abu Dawud 1920)"
"14233","(14233) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar; He prayed them in congregation."
"14234","(14234) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that if he missed the prayer with the imam With your knowledge, he combined the noon and afternoon prayers on his journey."
"14235","(14235) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you pray on your journey according to your knowledge, then pray one at a time. from each of them at its appointed time, and make for each one of them a call to prayer and an iqama."
"14236","(14236) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you pray while you are traveling, then if you wish, combine them, and if You wish to separate each one of them at its proper time."
"14237","(14237) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: My father never prayed with the imam. With your knowledge, and he used to bring them together, and he used to volunteer between them, and he used to do that from the soldiers until he came. Mecca"
"14238","(14238) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every prayer is to be performed at its appointed time."
"14239","(14239) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Maghrib and Isha’ prayers in Muzdalifah. (Ahmad 5/418, Darmi 1883)"
"14240","(14240) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kail, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He combined the two prayers with a plural prayer, then said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it. (Bukhari 1473 and Abu Dawud 1921)"
"14241","(14241) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Humaid, who said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab gathering in Morocco. And dinner in the plural."
"14242","(14242) Abu Bakr bin Ayash and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: I prayed with Abdullah Al-Maghrib in congregation, with the call to prayer and the iqamah, then we brought the evening prayer and we had dinner, then he led the evening prayer with us. With the call to prayer and the iqamah.

 Abu Bakr bin Ayyash added to it: Abu Ishaq said: So I met Abu Ja`far and informed him, and he said: And so do the people of The house."
"14243","(14243) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: It is Sunnah to combine the two."
"14244","(14244) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that when he departed from Arafat, he would only pray in The left side, and on the mountain, and that he used to combine Maghrib and the afterlife."
"14245","(14245) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He combines them together."
"14246","(14246) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; Ali brought them together together."
"14247","(14247) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, the Maghrib and the evening prayers with one call to prayer and two iqama, and he did not say the tasbih in between."
"14248","(14248) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Ayyub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers at Muzdalifah.

(Tabarani 3871, Ahmad 5/421)"
"14249","(14249) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr said: We continued with Ibn Umar until we came with a group, so he led the Maghrib and Isha prayers with us in one iqamah, then he left and said: This is how The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer in this place. (Muslim 291, Abu Dawud 1926)"
"14250","(14250) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with him Maghrib and Isha' prayers with one iqamah, and he said: I did it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"14251","(14251) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: Ali and Abdullah agreed that every prayer It is gathered with the adhan and iqamah."
"14252","(14252) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: I prayed in congregation with Sa’id bin Jubayr in the Maghrib. And dinner is done with one iqamah."
"14253","(14253) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He prayed the two prayers together with one iqamah."
"14254","(14254) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Hamid; Omar prayed the Maghrib and Isha prayers with the Iqamah."
"14255","(14255) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Al-Aswad established the prayer and prayed the Maghrib prayer in Muzdalifah, then he had dinner, then he prayed the evening prayer."
"14256","(14256) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, who said: I prayed behind Salim the sunset and evening prayers. In combination, with one call to prayer and two iqama, so I met Nafi’ and said to him: This is what Abdullah used to do? He said: Thus, I met Ata and said: I used to tell them: There is no prayer except by the Iqamah."
"14257","(14257) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Another sacrifice is due upon him."
"14258","(14258) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He owes another sacrifice."
"14259","(14259) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say that."
"14260","(14260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he shave his head before slaughtering his animal, he said: On him. Another guidance"
"14261","(14261) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: There is blood on him. Al-A’mash said: So I mentioned That was for Ibrahim, and he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, something similar."
"14262","(14262) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He slaughters a sheep, or feeds it. Six poor people, or fast for three days."
"14263","(14263) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Sadaqa bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: The time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted the people of Medina with Dhul-Halif, and with the people of Syria, Al-Juhfa, and with the people of Yemen with Yalamlam, and with the Qarn, with the people of Najd. Then a man said: For the people of Iraq? He said: There will be no Iraq on that day. (Bukhari 7344. Ahmad 2/140)"
"14264","(14264) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A man came and said: O Messenger of God, from Where will we get it? He said: The people of Medina are from Dhul-Halifah, the people of Syria are from Al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd are from Qarn, so he said: Ibn Omar: And they say: And the people of Yemen are from Yalamlam. (Bukhari 1525. Tirmidhi 831)"
"14265","(14265) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told his family Medina is Dhul-Halif, and for the people of the Levant is Al-Juhfah, and for the people of Yemen is Yalamam and Tahamah, and for the people of Najd is a horn, And the people of Iraq have their own race. (Muslim 840. Ahmad 3/333)"
"14266","(14266) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Tawus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a time for the people of Medina Dhul-Halifah, and for the people of the Levant Al-Juhfah, and for the people of We find that the Qarn al-Manazil, and for the people of Yemen to join each other, and he said: “Be gentle for them,” and for every one who came upon them other than them, of those who wanted Hajj and Umrah, and whoever is less than that, from wherever he originates, even the people of Mecca from Mecca.

(Bukhari 1526 and Abu Dawud 1735)"
"14267","(14267) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the aqeeq to the people of the East. (Tirmidhi 832, Abu Dawud 1737)"
"14268","(14268) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told his family Iraq has an ethnicity."
"14269","(14269) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Saeed bin al-Musayyab, he said: I said: To him: Where do we get our money from? He said: From the beginnings, from among them the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the decree for Hajj, and from among them he performed the decree for Umrah."
"14270","(14270) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Omar is a time for the people of Iraq to have the same race."
"14271","(14271) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said to the people of Iraq: Look at the shoes of a horn. Then they found her shoes with a vein, and a horn closer to Mecca than a vein. He said: So he made them for the people of Iraq."
"14272","(14272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He did not let anyone from his family go beyond the aqeeq unless he was in ihram."
"14273","(14273) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The limit for people is five: for the people of Medina with The Allies, and for the people of Mecca there is Tan'im, and for the people of the Levant is Al-Juhfah, and for the people of Yemen is Yalamlam, and for the people of Najd there is a Qarn, Or he said: The people of Iraq have a qarn. Then when it happened after that, they said to Ibn Abbas: We have no way to a qarn. He said: Its opposite is a dhat iraq."
"14274","(14274) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ammarah bin Zazan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; He was a member of his own race who was in ihram, and would not speak to any of the people until he circumambulated the Kaaba, except what was absolutely necessary."
"14275","(14275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, who said: I performed Hajj with Sa’id bin Jubayr and Mujahid, so we entered into ihram from Agate"
"14276","(14276) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: : I went out with Ibn Umar and he entered into ihram from Dhath Irq."
"14277","(14277) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Masruq say: For the people of Iraq is the aqeeq."
"14278","(14278) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Anas, who said: If you go out intending to perform Hajj, do not even say: I am a Hajj. He sighed, and he said: So I said: What should I say? He said: Say: I am a traveler."
"14279","(14279) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: Abdullah said: Who wanted this? The face, let him not say, “I am a pilgrim,” but rather the pilgrim in ihram, and let him say, “I am an expatriate.”"
"14280","(14280) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man performing Hajj and it seems to him that he should return before entering ihram. He said: There is no problem for him to return before entering ihram."
"14281","(14281) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If a man goes out He went to Mecca and then decided to return. He returned as long as he had not declared the ihram for Hajj."
"14282","(14282) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, who said: If he wants, he can do it, and if he wants, he can return."
"14283","(14283) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The hyenas of the son of Al-Zubayr bin Abdul Muttalib came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I want to perform Hajj. Should I stipulate? He said: Yes, stipulate. She said: How should I say? He said: Say: Here you are, O God, here you are, my home from the land where You imprisoned me. 

(Muslim 1061, Ahmad 1/337)"
"14284","(14284) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata was wearing the Talbiyah and was not a Mahram."
"14285","(14285) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man teaching a man what you wear and it is permissible, he said: There is no harm in it."
"14286","(14286) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in him."
"14287","(14287) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Our people used to teach us. That"
"14288","(14288) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, who said: They did not see any harm in him."
"14289","(14289) Ali bin Musir and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin narrated to us. Sabit, on the authority of Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’a Al-Makhzoumi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This will continue. The nations are well as long as they venerate this sacred thing as it should be venerated, but if they neglect it, they will be destroyed. (Ibn Majah 3110; Ahmad 4/347)"
"14290","(14290) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: This is a sanctuary - meaning Mecca - God made it sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and placed these two woods on It was permissible for anyone before me, and it is not permissible for anyone after me, and it was not permissible for me except for an hour of the day, and it will not break its thorns, and it will not be dispersed. They hunted, and their cells were not to be separated, nor were their shots raised except for a singer. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, the people of Mecca are They have no patience for Al-Idhkhir, for their livelihood and for their children. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Except Al-Idhkhir.

(Bukhari 1587, Muslim 986)"
"14291","(14291) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, who said: Omar said: O family Mecca, fear God in the sanctuary of God. Do you know who lives in this country? There were the sons of so-and-so in it, and they made lawful its sacred places, and they were destroyed. And there were the sons of so-and-so, and they made unlawful its sacred places, and they were destroyed, until He mentioned whatever of the Arab tribes God wished for him to be mentioned, then he said: Because committing ten sins with my knees is more beloved to me than doing This is one sin."
"14292","(14292) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever intends an evil deed will not It will be recorded for him until he does it, and if he were to go to Aden and refused to be killed at the Sacred Mosque, God would make him taste the torment. Painful, then he recited: {And whoever rejects it with heresy commits injustice}"
"14293","(14293) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sulayman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The sanctuary is forbidden in The seven heavens are the size of the earth, and the Holy House is sanctified in the seven heavens the size of the earth."
"14294","(14294) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: When the season was With the Jahiliyyah, they left, and no one remained in Mecca. A thief remained behind, so he took pieces of gold and put them away. Then he went in to take something more, and when he entered his head, they closed the door, and they found his head in the house, and he was outside, so they threw him out. For the dogs and repair the house."
"14295","(14295) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that he had two tents; One of them is in the Sacred Mosque and the other is in the Sacred Mosque, so if he wants to pray, he prays in the one in the Sacred Mosque, and if she has The one in need of his family came to the one in need, and was told about that? He said: Indeed, Mecca is Mecca."
"14296","(14296) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I said to him: Why does he not scavenge a lion? He said: You turn it from the shadow to the sun, and settle in its place."
"14297","(14297) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Sa’d, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who heard Abu Huraira says, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: He will destroy the Ka’bah with two stalks from Ethiopia.

(Bukhari 1591, Muslim 57)"
"14298","(14298) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abi Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student said: It is as if I am looking at a man from Ethiopia, bald, deaf, with brown legs, sitting on it while he is He destroys it."
"14299","(14299) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who heard Ibn Amr say: It is as if I am in him. A bald, handsome man was standing over it and demolishing it with his wipes. When Ibn al-Zubayr demolished it, I started to look at its surface. Ibn Amr did not see her.

(Ahmed 220)"
"14300","(14300) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Ibn al-Zubayr agreed to demolish it We left for Mina as three, awaiting the punishment."
"14301","(14301) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kulayl, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, on the authority of Aleem Al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, said: This house will be burned at the hands of a man from the Al-Zubayr family."
"14302","(14302) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: When the house was demolished, a rock was found in it. It is written: I am God, the one who blesses you. I shaped it on the day I shaped the sun and the moon. I surrounded it with seven pure angels. I blessed it. For its family in the fat and fat, it will not disappear until the woods disappear, meaning the two mountains, and the first to solve them Welcome"
"14303","(14303) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Salma bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, who said: When the house was destroyed, he came He poured water and overturned one of the stones of the House, and behold, there was written on it: I am God, the One who weeps. I shaped it on the day I shaped the two mountains. It was built on top of seven Hanafi properties, neither Jews nor Christians."
"14304","(14304) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: narrated to me someone who read a book in a hole in a roof. The House, or the lowest place of Abraham: I am God, the One who weeps for you. I have built seven noble kingdoms upon it and inside it. I have blessed it. For his family in meat and water, and I have made provision for his family in three ways, and it is not permissible to deprive him of the first one to make him welcome."
"14305","(14305) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Mina, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr He says: If you see the Quraysh demolishing the House, then they built it and roofed it, then if you are able to die, then die."
"14306","(14306) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, who said: I was holding the bridle of an animal. Abdullah bin Amr, and he said: How would you do if you demolished this house and did not leave one stone upon another? They said: And we follow Islam? He said: We are Muslims. I said: Then what? He said: Then it will be built as best as it has ever been, so if you see Mecca, it will be filled with towers, and you will see the building rising to the tops of the mountains. Know that the matter has overshadowed you."
"14307","(14307) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: Enjoy this House before it is raised, for it will be raised and demolished twice, and raised on the third time."
"14308","(14308) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If we had had the means, I would have demolished the Kaaba, built it, and given it two doors. A door through which people enter, and a door through which they leave. He said: When Ibn al-Zubayr took charge, he demolished it, so he made it two doors. And it was like that, so when Al-Hajjaj came to power, he demolished it and rebuilt the first one. (Bukhari 1583, Muslim 968)"
"14309","(14309) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah bin Adiy, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the shepherds to stone one day and leave another day. (Abu Dawud 1970, Ibn Majah 3036)"
"14310","(14310) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted the shepherds to shoot at night. (Bayhaqi 151)"
"14311","(14311) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ata’; Omar gave permission for the shepherds to spend the night in Mina. He said: Did you mention that to Al-Zuhri? He said: The shepherds throw stones at night and do not stay overnight."
"14312","(14312) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to make stoning stones popular among the camel herders, ordering those with him to throw stones when the sun had passed, and then They go to the camels, and those with the camels come and throw stones, then they stay until they throw them the next day when they are gone. The sun"
"14313","(14313) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He rides When the walker stones the Jamarat."
"14314","(14314) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A pedestrian should not ride until he has completed the rituals. All of them"
"14315","(14315) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A pedestrian should not ride until he has stopped."
"14316","(14316) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’; Like him"
"14317","(14317) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman, who said: I heard Mujahid and Sa`id bin Jubayr said: We used to see Abdullah bin Abbas, when he stoned the Jamarat, raise his hands until they were equal to his head. The whiteness of his armpits can be seen, and his pebbles are like fresh hazelnuts."
"14318","(14318) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he throws At the Jamarat, let him raise his hands until the whites of his armpits can be seen."
"14319","(14319) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Al-Walid ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; When he stoned the Jamarat, he would move forward in front of it, supplicate to God, raise his hand, and We would raise with him. He would not lower his hand until We got bored and put our hands down, and it was as it was."
"14320","(14320) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The hands are raised when The stones"
"14321","(14321) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to say: The hands should be raised when The two Jamratina."
"14322","(14322) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Ibn Abu Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, they said: The hands should be raised at the pebbles."
"14323","(14323) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who performs Hajj and dies before completing his rituals. He said: He will perform the remainder of his rituals on his behalf."
"14324","(14324) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Nayk, who said: I asked Tawus about a woman who had died. Does she have any remaining rituals left? He said: It will be paid for, and I asked Al-Qasim? He said: I have no knowledge of what Tawus said. God said: (Do not bear the burden of one who bears the burden of another)"
"14325","(14325) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The place of the Ka’bah was weeping, and nothing else. What??"
"14326","(14326) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I heard Ikrimah saying: He cried all the time. The House, and Mecca and beyond that."
"14327","(14327) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: It was called Wecca because people come to it from all sides as pilgrims."
"14328","(14328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr being asked: Why was it called Bakkah? He said: Because they cry over it."
"14329","(14329) Muhammad bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, he said: It was called Weeping because people cry over it."
"14330","(14330) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Utba ibn Qays, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Mecca wept with tears, The male is like the female."
"14331","(14331) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was called Bakkah because the people They make each other cry, and it is permissible in it what is not permissible in any other."
"14332","(14332) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Atiya, who said: The place of the House wept, and what was around it became Mecca."
"14333","(14333) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Majliz; That Gabriel brought Abraham to Arafat, and he said: Did you know? He said: Yes, he said: Hence it was named Arafat."
"14334","(14334) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was named Arafat because Gabriel was there. He shows Ibrahim the rituals and says: Did you know? Then he shows it and says: Did you know? So it was named Arafat."
"14335","(14335) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is blessed. It means Zamzam, food of any kind."
"14336","(14336) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said about Zamzam water: It is food for those who taste it, and a cure for those who are sick."
"14337","(14337) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abi Al-Abbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We used to call Zamzam Shabaya, and we claim that it is a blessing for our families."
"14338","(14338) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: A man from the Levant narrated to me, on the authority of Ka’b, He said: I heard him say: Indeed, in the revealed Book of God: One hundred Zamzam water is food and a cure for illness."
"14339","(14339) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Qais bin Kurkum, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas and said: Tell me about Zamzam water? He said: I tell you with knowledge: Do not shun, do not bleed, do not disparage food of any kind, and cure anyone who is sick."
"14340","(14340) Saeed bin Zakaria and Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’mil, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One hundred Zamzam for what he drank for him. (Ahmad 3/357, Bayhaqi 148)"
"14341","(14341) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Othman, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: His intention."
"14342","(14342) Yahya bin Saeed and Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: His intention."
"14343","(14343) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; They said: His intention."
"14344","(14344) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: I set out for Umrah in Rajab, and I wanted to perform the ihram for Umrah, so I did. By Hajj, so I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about that? He laughed and said: There is nothing wrong with you, and Al-Hasan said the same as Saeed bin Jubayr said."
"14345","(14345) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who wanted to perform Umrah but was willing to perform Hajj, he said: Hajj is not obligatory for him."
"14346","(14346) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus; Concerning a man who performs Umrah on the day of Arafah, circumambulates the Kaaba and performs Sa’i between al-Safa and al-Marwah. He said: He should not go to women. And the people stand according to your custom."
"14347","(14347) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in it."
"14348","(14348) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Khalid bin Arara, on the authority of Ali; That Abraham, peace be upon him, said to his son: Make me a stone. He said: So he went, then he came and rode it, and he said: Where is this from? He said: He who did not trust in your building brought it to me. Gabriel from the heavens brought it to me."
"14349","(14349) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The stone is one of the stones of Paradise. And had he not touched him of the impurities of the people of the pre-Islamic era, he would not have touched anyone except that he was healed."
"14350","(14350) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The stone came down from Paradise, and it is whiter than snow, and nothing darkened it except the sins of the children of Adam."
"14351","(14351) Abdul narrated to us, on the authority of?? Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, said: Ka’b was asked about the Black Stone? He said: A stone from the stones of Paradise."
"14352","(14352) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The stone is one of the stones of Paradise."
"14353","(14353) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sawadah bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Perform this Hajj. House, and hold this stone. By God, it will be lifted up, or some command from the heavens will befall it, if they were two stones. They were brought down from Paradise, then one of them will be raised and the other will be raised, and if it is not as I said, then whoever passes by my grave should say: This The grave of Abdullah bin Amr Al-Kaddhab."
"14354","(14354) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ziyad, a client of Banu Makhzum, who said: Had he not touched The stone is one of the sins of the children of Adam. No one who has committed a sin touches it except that he is healed."
"14355","(14355) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {And whoever honors the rituals of God, they are from the strengthening of hearts} He said: in seeking permission, seeking approval, and seeking esteem."
"14356","(14356) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Musa, who said in the Almighty’s saying: {And whoever He magnifies the rituals of God, for they are the strength of hearts. He said: Standing according to custom is one of the rituals of God, and in a combination of the rituals of God, and the body is The rituals of God, and shaving is one of the rituals of God, and archery is one of the rituals of God, so whoever honors it, it is from the strengthening of hearts."
"14357","(14357) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Habib the teacher, on the authority of Ata’; That he was asked about the rituals of God? He said: The sanctities of God, avoiding the wrath of God and following His obedience, for these are the rituals of God."
"14358","(14358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid: (And who magnifies the rituals of God) he said: Her greatness and approval."
"14359","(14359) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to descend the lower ones first."
"14360","(14360) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, that Abdullah Ibn Al-Sa'ib narrated it; Omar bin Al-Khattab came to Mecca and settled at the highest point of Mecca."
"14361","(14361) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim, Ibn Abi Bazza, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Masoud; He stayed at Umm Hani's house."
"14362","(14362) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He stayed at the house of Umm Hani’ during the month of Ramadan."
"14363","(14363) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; Aisha used to come to Mecca in Al-Abtah, and she would be called to the hall but she refused."
"14364","(14364) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If the body reaches the Sacred Sanctuary, it has passed."
"14365","(14365) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Every sacrificial animal that enters the Sanctuary has paid in full on behalf of its owner, except This is the sacrifice of the animal, for he must have something that he has forgotten, with which he will be permissible on the Day of Sacrifice."
"14366","(14366) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid that they said: Al-Qarin and Al-Tamattu’. Their guidance and tawaaf are the same."
"14367","(14367) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Jafar; Ibn Abbas and Ali bin Hussein were not widowed."
"14368","(14368) Abbad ibn al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: If he wishes, he may sand, and if he wishes, he may not sand. He said: He was generous in his view, and if he wished, he would sand, and if he wanted, he would not sand, and sand was more beloved to him."
"14369","(14369) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdulaziz, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who forgets sand, he said: There is nothing on it."
"14370","(14370) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was not a widow when he arrived from Mecca."
"14371","(14371) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, Sa’id bin Jubayr said: The person who is besieged is not permissible except with blood."
"14372","(14372) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A person who has been confined is not permissible except with blood."
"14373","(14373) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He fasts for ten days."
"14374","(14374) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The voice should not be raised when reciting recitation. On the evening of Arafah, at noon and afternoon."
"14375","(14375) Hammad bin Masadhi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I attended Ibrahim bin Hisham on the day he recognized him, and he agreed. He gathered together, so he spoke out loud with the Qur’anic Quran, and Salem said with his hand, “Shut up.”"
"14376","(14376) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, or Tawoos, who said: The imam should not speak loudly. On the evening of Friday, even if that coincides with the day of Friday."
"14377","(14377) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, similarly, he said: And he saw Sufyan."
"14378","(14378) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, ?? Al-Zuhri; The Imam does not recite the Qur’an recitation out loud during the noon or afternoon prayers on the day of Arafah."
"14379","(14379) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to bring his servants into the sanctuary without being in a state of ihram, and he would benefit from them."
"14380","(14380) Omar bin Ali bin Ata bin Muqaddam told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa; That his father used to let his boys enter the sanctuary, even though they were not ihram."
"14381","(14381) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in a man preventing his servant from entering ihram, and Ibn Sirin said: I do not know that this is a form of kindness."
"14382","(14382) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim taking his two servants out for Hajj, but no They are deprived of Dhul-Halifah, they are deprived of the one in front of that."
"14383","(14383) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Ibn Zayd’s servants taking out the village. So they will go with him from Dhul-Halif."
"14384","(14384) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who hurried for two days and went to hunting ground. He said: He did not see anything wrong with him."
"14385","(14385) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man who was in a hurry for two days, fishing? He said: If he leaves the sanctuary, there is no problem."
"14386","(14386) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to bring them back to the appointed times. Those who enter Mecca without Ihram."
"14387","(14387) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Abu Al-Khalil wrote to Sa’id bin Jubayr informing him: Only those who enter it without ihram enter ihram from Mecca."
"14388","(14388) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: My eyes saw Ibn Abbas returns them to the appointed times."
"14389","(14389) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zayd passed by a woman who was crying. He said: What makes you cry? She said: I passed my meeqaat while I was menstruating, so I passed it, but I did not perform ihram. He said: Why? She said: He forbade me. He said: So go out and I will treat you with my family from another place."
"14390","(14390) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who entered Mecca neither as a Hajj nor as a Umrah performer, and he was afraid that if he went out at the appointed time he would miss him. He said: He will perform Il-Hilal from his place. And he did not mention blood."
"14391","(14391) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Bura, who said: A man entered Mecca, wearing his clothes, and attended Hajj. He feared that if he returned, he would miss it, so Ibn al-Zubayr ordered him to perform the Ihram from where he was, and when he had completed the Hajj, he would go out at the appointed time. So he made his Umrah come to fruition."
"14392","(14392) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who was ignorant until he entered Mecca. The greatness of his statement was that he would come from his place, and Al-Hasan said: It was only He returns to his limit to complete it, unless he fears missing it. If he fears missing it, he returns to his place and moves on, and nothing. Aliyah"
"14393","(14393) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He descends from his place and there is blood on him."
"14394","(14394) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar used to perform Hajj and would not slaughter anything until he returned."
"14395","(14395) Abdi told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, who said: Nafi’ bin Jubayr said: I have never sacrificed in Mecca."
"14396","(14396) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to perform Hajj and they had papers and gold, but what They would slaughter something, but they would leave it for fear that it would distract them from any of the rituals."
"14397","(14397) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; She used to perform Hajj, so she did not sacrifice on behalf of her brother’s sons."
"14398","(14398) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Abi al-Darda’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We will not pray here, and he will not sacrifice on the Day of Resurrection. The slaughter"
"14399","(14399) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Wabara; Al-Aswad and Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid used to perform Hajj but did not perform the sacrifice."
"14400","(14400) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of a statement; Alqamiya used to perform Hajj but did not perform the sacrifice."
"14401","(14401) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas; He did not sacrifice during the Hajj, so when it was the days of Tashreeq, he said: Buy cows, prepare them, and we will provide for them. We traveled"
"14402","(14402) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutanir al-Musli, on the authority of Bura ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of a sheikh from the orphanage, He said: We were with Saad in Mina and he did not sacrifice, then he sent to his neighbors: Give us food from your sacrifice."
"14403","(14403) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Kulayb bin Wa’il, on the authority of his uncle Qays, on the authority of Saad, something similar."
"14404","(14404) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I performed three Hajjs, and I did not shed any blood."
"14405","(14405) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled; He was with Salem in Hajj, so he did not sacrifice a manna."
"14406","(14406) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’ and Mujahid, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Whoever performs Hajj and sacrifices Hadi, he returned to his family for Hajj and Umrah."
"14407","(14407) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who leaves al-Safa and al-Marwa, he said: A blood sacrifice is upon him."
"14408","(14408) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; Dawud bin Abi Asim came and left Safa and Marwa, and Ata said: Spill blood, and Tawoos said: Enter to perform Umrah."
"14409","(14409) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim said: If he forgets to circumambulate between Safa and Marwah while he is a Hajj, then he must perform Hajj, and if he was performing Umrah, he must do it. Umrah, and nothing suffices for it except tawaf between them."
"14410","(14410) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If he wishes, he may run between the two rows. And the narration, and if he wanted to, he could not do it."
"14411","(14411) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He did not consider anyone who did not walk between Safa and Marwa anything. I said: He has left something of the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Not against him, and he used to issue fatwas with blood in public."
"14412","(14412) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: God has not completed the Hajj of one who does not He walked between As-Safa and Al-Marwah, then I recited: (Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God.)"
"14413","(14413) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Safiyy ibn Shaybah; She heard Aisha and it was said to her: Some of your brother’s daughters hate them to wear their jewellery, and they are forbidden. So she swore that she would wear all her jewelry."
"14414","(14414) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; The wives and daughters of Abdullah bin Omar used to wear jewellery, but they were in ihram."
"14415","(14415) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They disliked women being interrupted in the lawful manner. And the ihram."
"14416","(14416) Hakam Al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Zubaidi, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about jewelry and silk. For a mahram, should you wear it? He said: If she wears it while it is lawful, then let her wear it while it is forbidden."
"14417","(14417) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about the forbidden item: What jewelry do you wear? He said: The ring."
"14418","(14418) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman in ihram wears hidden jewelry. And its tawāriyah."
"14419","(14419) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of al-Aswad, and his They said: The woman in ihram should wear whatever she used to wear, and this is permissible, such as her shame and her shame."
"14420","(14420) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: I asked Ibn Al-Aswad: What should a woman in ihram wear? The jewelry? He said: She was not wearing it while she was wearing it."
"14421","(14421) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was disliked for a woman in ihram to wear Al-Hilli Al-Mashhour, he said: I said: What about the necklace? He said: If it is a joint contract, then no."
"14422","(14422) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A woman in ihram should not adorn herself, nor should she use kohl. For her adornment."
"14423","(14423) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked jewelry for a mahram woman."
"14424","(14424) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was disliked for a woman to wear a mahram. The jewellery."
"14425","(14425) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about him, meaning The ring is for a person in ihram; He said: There is no problem, we used to walk around the Kaaba while it was on us, and we would preserve it for the week."
"14426","(14426) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a ring for a person in ihram."
"14427","(14427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no problem. With a ring for the person in ihram."
"14428","(14428) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Mujahid; He said: There is no harm in a ring for a person in ihram."
"14429","(14429) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a ring for a person in ihram."
"14430","(14430) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah wearing his ring. And it is forbidden."
"14431","(14431) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw a seal on Sa’id bin Jubayr. He is in Ihram, and he is obligated to give."
"14432","(14432) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a ring for a person in ihram."
"14433","(14433) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; It was disliked for a woman in ihram to cover her face, and there was no harm in her covering her face, and he disliked wearing gloves."
"14434","(14434) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman in ihram may wear whatever clothing she wants, except The burqa and gloves."
"14435","(14435) They narrated?? Ibn Fudail, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, who said: A woman in ihram may wear whatever clothing she wants, except the burqa. And the gloves."
"14436","(14436) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: She may wear whatever she wants, except the burqa."
"14437","(14437) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata, who said: She should wear gloves and trousers, and not wear a burqa. She does not wear a mask, and she may wear whatever clothing she wants, except a garment with a dusting of wool over her, or saffron."
"14438","(14438) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He disliked the burqa and gloves for women in ihram."
"14439","(14439) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id and Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: No. She must wear gloves, and do not wear clothing that has been touched by rice or saffron."
"14440","(14440) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Salma ibn Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The woman in ihram wears gloves and trousers."
"14441","(14441) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the gloves? They said: There is no harm in it."
"14442","(14442) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He forbids women in ihram from wearing gloves and niqab, and from clothing that has been touched by wool and saffron. (Bukhari 1838 and Abu Dawud 1822)"
"14443","(14443) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A woman in ihram may wear whatever she wants. Clothes, except the burqa and gloves, and do not wear a niqab."
"14444","(14444) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah used to bury his face in his garment while he Muharram."
"14445","(14445) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm if the wind hurts you while you are in ihram to lift your garment. To your face, and there is no harm for a woman, if the smell bothers her, to lower her dress over her face."
"14446","(14446) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, while we were in Ihram, so when we met the knees, we pulled our clothes over our heads over our faces. When we crossed We raised it.

(Abu Dawud 1829, Darqutni 262)"
"14447","(14447) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the wind disturbs a pilgrim in ihram, there is no harm in him raising his head. His garment is from between his hands and he covers his forehead with it."
"14448","(14448) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus, who said: There is no harm in covering your face while you are in Ihram. And your nose while you are in ihram, to your forehead."
"14449","(14449) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The person in ihram lifts his garment when he is lying down. To her eyes, and the woman in ihram draws her garment over her face."
"14450","(14450) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Farafasi bin Umayr said: I saw Othman covering his face while he was in ihram."
"14451","(14451) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: His face is hidden. With his garment up to the hair of his head, and Abu Al-Zubair pointed out that he had his garment up to his head."
"14452","(14452) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The face and what is above it from the head. No one should cover the chin or above."
"14453","(14453) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; When he slept, he would cover his face to the ends of his hair."
"14454","(14454) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Farafsiyah; He saw Othman, Zaid, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam covering their faces while they were in ihram."
"14455","(14455) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Al-Farafsi, he said: I saw Uthman He covered his face with his garment while he was in ihram."
"14456","(14456) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Salim ibn Mahan, he said: Omar ibn Abd Al-Aziz permits the ihram to cover his lips below his nose."
"14457","(14457) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The person in ihram covers his face up to the eyebrows. And he said: This is the saying of Sufyan."
"14458","(14458) Abduh bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Hatib, on the authority of who saw Othman was in ihram, covering his face."
"14459","(14459) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Farafsi, He said: I saw Uthman, Zaid, and Ibn al-Zubayr covering their faces while they were in ihram, to the point of cutting their hair."
"14460","(14460) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw a man in ihram who was seeking shade with a stick, so he said: Offer the sacrifice to the one to whom you entered ihram."
"14461","(14461) Abd Allah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, he said: I went out with Omar, and what I saw him wandering around until he returned, and I said to him, or it was said to him: What was he seeking shade for? He said: He used to place the nat`a on the tree and take shade from it."
"14462","(14462) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: There were companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they sacrifice when they enter ihram."
"14463","(14463) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of his brother Ismail bin Rashid, who said: We performed Hajj and Amr ibn Maymun was with us. A severe cold struck us, so he was covering his head while we were in ihram."
"14464","(14464) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ata’, and on the authority of his father, who said: The person in ihram should take shade. With the lute and his hand, from heat and cold."
"14465","(14465) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: My father used to make The garment is on the bearing, providing shade with it."
"14466","(14466) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He did not see any harm in the pilgrim in ihram seeking shade from the sun."
"14467","(14467) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Matar, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil; Like him"
"14468","(14468) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd bin Rifa’i, who said: I saw Mujahid while he was in ihram, and on His journey is like energy."
"14469","(14469) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Shabib; That Aisha was asked about a woman in ihram who was struck by a cold? She said: He says this with his clothes. And he raised him above his head."
"14470","(14470) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; By the same to him"
"14471","(14471) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib Al-Muallem, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a person in ihram who was caught by rain and covered his head? He said: A ransom of fasting, or alms, or ritual sacrifice."
"14472","(14472) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman, who said: I heard Dhar asking Abraham about what happened to a muhrim. Heavens, how is it made? He said: He raises his mask over his head, and does not cover his head with it."
"14473","(14473) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The first person to know about insight was Ibn Abbas."
"14474","(14474) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, who said: I saw Amr bin Harith giving a sermon. The day he was known, and the people had gathered to him."
"14475","(14475) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-A’mash, he said: I saw Abu Wa’il and our companions. They will sit on the Day of Arafah and talk as they talk on all other days."
"14476","(14476) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala; He saw Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab on the evening of Arafat, leaning his back toward al-Maqsoor, and facing the Levant until sunset. The sun"
"14477","(14477) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awanna, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, who said: What He used to attend the Grand Mosque on the eve of Arafat, except for those who had attended it before that."
"14478","(14478) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: They were asking Muhammad about coming to the mosque. On the eve of Arafah? He said: I don't know of any harm in him. He was sitting in his house, and his conversation that evening was the same as his conversation in all other matters. The days"
"14479","(14479) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad. He said: I asked them about the meeting on the eve of Arafat? They said: Hadith."
"14480","(14480) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about the definition? He said: The definition is of Mecca."
"14481","(14481) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bukair ibn Amir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one known as Mecca."
"14482","(14482) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The one known as Mecca is only"
"14483","(14483) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: We were not recognized except in our mosques."
"14484","(14484) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail al-Azraq, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: The one known as Mecca is only the one who is known as Mecca."
"14485","(14485) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Indeed, the most deserving of The men remained in their homes on the Day of Arafat."
"14486","(14486) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar, he said: Muhammad bin Sirin narrated to us, he said: You have seen us in the time of Ziyad and what We disavow the eve of Arafat from all other eves."
"14487","(14487) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Al-Hakam, who said: The one who recognizes a heresy."
"14488","(14488) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin; They did not visit the mosque on the eve of Arafat."
"14489","(14489) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He disliked visiting the Kaaba on the days of Tashreeq, meaning after the obligatory prayer."
"14490","(14490) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you visit the Ka’bah on the Day of Sacrifice, do not return to it. Until you flee."
"14491","(14491) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid; He disliked visiting him during the days of Tashreeq, meaning after the obligatory prayer."
"14492","(14492) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray in prayer every night."
"14493","(14493) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to come to the House in the days of the East, and no one did that."
"14494","(14494) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you visit the Ka’bah on the days of Tashreeq Every day is better."
"14495","(14495) Abu Khaled and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: They informed me. Abu Talha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, linked Hajj and Umrah. (Ahmad 4/28, Abu Ali 1412)"
"14496","(14496) Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam, he said: We were walking with Othman, and he heard a man greeting them all, and Othman said: Who is this? They said: Ali. He said: Then Othman came to him and said: Did you not know that I forbade this? He said: Yes, but I would not let the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do what you said. (Bukhari 1563. Ahmad 1/135)"
"14497","(14497) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: We went out as pilgrims and with us was Al-Sabbi bin Ma’abad. He said: So he entered into ihram for Hajj and Umrah. He said: So we came to Omar and he mentioned that to him, and he said: I have been guided by the Sunnah of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 1795. Ahmad 1/25)"
"14498","(14498) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd ibn Abi Lubab, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, on the authority of Al-Sabi ibn Ma’abad, About Omar; In the same way (Ibn Majah 2970. Ahmad 1/25)"
"14499","(14499) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Al-Sabi bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Omar; In the same way (Ahmad 1/37 Tayalisi 58)"
"14500","(14500) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Imran, he said: I performed Hajj with My master, I went to Umm Salamah and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: O family of Muhammad, welcome his life. Hajj (Ahmad 6/297, Abu Ali 7011)"
"14501","(14501) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, linked Hajj and Umrah, and performed one circumambulation for them. (Tirmidhi 947. Ahmad 3/381)"
"14502","(14502) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, he said: Hamid bin Hilal told me, he said: I heard Mutarrif bin Abdullah say: Imran bin Husayn told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Hajj and Umrah, then he did not discontinue it. About him, and no book was sent down prohibiting him. (Muslim 1688, Ahmad 4/428)"
"14503","(14503) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, will perform the Talbiyah with both of them: I will perform Talbiyah with Hajj and Umrah together. (Bukhari 1551, Abu Dawud 1792)"
"14504","(14504) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas; He heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: I will fulfill your Umrah and Hajj. (Muslim 214. Abu Dawud 1792)"
"14505","(14505) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Qatada saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only performed the prayer because he was informed that he would not perform Hajj after her."
"14506","(14506) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I heard the companions of Muhammad pray May God bless him and grant him peace, they may perform Umrah and Hajj together."
"14507","(14507) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Kathir bin Jumhan, who said: We went out as pilgrims and with us A man from the people of the mountain had never performed Hajj, so he performed Hajj and his life, and our companions criticized him for that. He said: So we camped soon. From Ibn Umar, he said: So we said to him: There is with us a man from the people of the mountain who had never performed Hajj, so he qualified for Hajj and ‘Umrah, so he disgraced him. Our companions, what is his expiation? He said: His expiation is that he returns with two rewards and you return with one."
"14508","(14508) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I will fulfill your Umrah and Hajj together.

(Abu Dawud 1792. An-Nasa’i 3709)"
"14509","(14509) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hamid, and Musab, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will meet you with your life and your Hajj. (Ahmad 3/111, Hamidi 1215)"
"14510","(14510) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, we only see Hajj. (Bukhari 294. Muslim 119)"
"14511","(14511) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted those who joined the Hajj. (Bukhari 1560, Ahmad 6/207)"
"14512","(14512) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, singled out Hajj was performed for forty years later, and they were the most steadfast in following its Sunnah, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman."
"14513","(14513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of His father; That Abu Bakr and Omar were stripped, Sufyan added: and Othman."
"14514","(14514) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Al-Hajj singled out Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman. And Alqamah, and the lions."
"14515","(14515) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I asked Suleiman bin Yassar about combining Hajj and Umrah? He said: We do not like to mix anything with our Hajj."
"14516","(14516) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Spread out Hajj, and abandon this statement of your uncles, meaning Ibn Abbas."
"14517","(14517) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated the Qur’an and entertainment, and said: Abstraction is more beloved to me."
"14518","(14518) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salih al-Ukli, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Stripping is more beloved to me."
"14519","(14519) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar; It is the Hajj of his entire caliphate, and he performs the Hajj individually."
"14520","(14520) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud: “Nusakan, I would love for each one of them to be well-groomed and travelled.” He said: “The lions traveled for eighty days between Hajj.” And his age, he did not combine them, and Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad traveled for sixty days between Hajj and his age, and he did not combine them. Between them."
"14521","(14521) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: I went out with Abraham and with us were some of our companions. So they all entered into ihram and performed Hajj."
"14522","(14522) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ziyad bin Malik; Ali and Ibn Masoud said about Al-Qarin: He performs two circumambulations."
"14523","(14523) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, who said: If You have combined Hajj and Umrah, so perform two tawafs, and make two sa'ys."
"14524","(14524) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: He will go around two circuits. And he strives with two efforts."
"14525","(14525) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Al-Qarin performs tawaf. Two circumambulations, and two sa'ys."
"14526","(14526) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Qarin circumambulates. Two circuses."
"14527","(14527) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, and Hammad about Al-Qarin? They said: He goes around two times, and he runs two times."
"14528","(14528) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning Al-Qarin, he said: Two circumambulations and two journeys."
"14529","(14529) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated them once."
"14530","(14530) Yahya bin Abi Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He swore to me None of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated for Hajj and Umrah, except one circumambulation."
"14531","(14531) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If Hajj and Umrah are combined with one circumambulation, One sa'i, and when combined, two circumambulations and two sa'is."
"14532","(14532) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Salim, he said: When he combined Between Hajj and Umrah, he must perform one tawaf and one sa’i."
"14533","(14533) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A tawaf is sufficient."
"14534","(14534) Ibn Abi Ghaniya told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you present a qarin or a mutati’, it is sufficient for you. One sa’i between Safa and Marwah. If you are a second sa’i, then delay that until the Day of Sacrifice."
"14535","(14535) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He performed one circumambulation for them."
"14536","(14536) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri (h) and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan. They said: He performs tawaf."
"14537","(14537) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far (h) and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He goes around."
"14538","(14538) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Ata’, and Tawoos. They said: It roams. The qarin is a circumambulation."
"14539","(14539) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; That Ali used to forbid women from wearing the niqab while they were sacred, but to let the garment fall over their faces completely."
"14540","(14540) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The woman rejects The woman in ihram must cover her face, and do not wear a niqab."
"14541","(14541) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Yahya, and Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Do not cover a woman in ihram."
"14542","(14542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Umm Shabib, on the authority of Aisha; She disliked the niqab for a woman in a state of ihram and kohl, and made it permissible to wear socks."
"14543","(14543) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He disliked the niqab and gloves for women in ihram."
"14544","(14544) Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Do not wear the niqab."
"14545","(14545) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about the niqab for women in ihram? They thought about it and said: You should turn your face to God."
"14546","(14546) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade it, meaning the niqab."
"14547","(14547) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’aib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God stood May God’s prayers and peace be upon him at the second Jamarat, longer than he stopped at the first Jamarat. Then he came to Jamarat al-Aqabah. He threw it away and did not stop there."
"14548","(14548) Yahya bin Sulaym Al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Aswad bin Khalaf, who said: I realized that people were getting some water when they set out to throw stones at the Jamarat, as long as they stood at the two Jamarat."
"14549","(14549) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He stood with Ibn Abbas as much as one of the seven surahs. He said: I said: Among the people is some who slows down the recitation and among them is some who speeds up? He said: Like my reading? He said: I said: You are light in recitation. He said: Like your recitation."
"14550","(14550) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ali Al-Azdi informed me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Like the hadith of Abdullah Iya."
"14551","(14551) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I stood with Amr bin Shuaib and Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, and they did not... Yatila, and I stood with a donation equal to the surah of Hajj."
"14552","(14552) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr and Ibrahim. And a peacock, and Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, who prolong their standing at the pebbles."
"14553","(14553) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn Umar used to stand at the two Jamarat. How much does a man recite Surah Al-Baqarah?"
"14554","(14554) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Ibn Umar used to stand at the Jamarat for a period of time. The man recites Surah Al-Baqarah."
"14555","(14555) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj; Ataa stopped at the burning coal for the same amount of time as a man reads a surah out of a hundred."
"14556","(14556) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar; Because they hated to be left from the soil of the sanctuary into the sanctuary, or to enter from the dust of the sanctuary into the sanctuary."
"14557","(14557) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Abi Al-Furat Al-Makki narrated to us, on the authority of his father; When Ibn al-Zubayr demolished the Kaaba and built it, he hated to build on it from the soil of the solution."
"14558","(14558) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’; He disliked it, meaning that he should take out the dirt from the sanctuary to the sanctuary."
"14559","(14559) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid who said: Do not circumambulate the Kaaba unless you are On ablution."
"14560","(14560) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He would not perform any of the rituals unless he had performed ablution."
"14561","(14561) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ata’, and Al-Hasan; They disliked for a man to circumambulate without being pure."
"14562","(14562) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, Hammad, Mansur, and Suleiman about the man who circumambulates. By staying at home without purity? They saw no harm in him."
"14563","(14563) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They did not see any harm in a man circling between Safa and Marwah without performing ablution, and ablution was the most beloved. To them."
"14564","(14564) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man enters ihram while wearing a shirt, then he does not He takes it from his head, splits it, then comes out of it."
"14565","(14565) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah and Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shaabi said: It breaks it."
"14566","(14566) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id (H) and on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: When he enters ihram, he must A shirt, let it be broken."
"14567","(14567) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Qatadah, who said: Yashqihu."
"14568","(14568) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: He should take it off by his feet."
"14569","(14569) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to say: Who He enters ihram while wearing a shirt, let him take it off and not tear it apart."
"14570","(14570) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will remove it."
"14571","(14571) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’li, on the authority of his father, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take it off, and do in your Umrah what you did in your Hajj, meaning, make a forehead. It was on her.

(Bukhari 1789. Muslim 10)"
"14572","(14572) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: He will remove it."
"14573","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad told us Ibn Abi Shaybah said:

(14573) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet prayed May God bless her and grant her peace, and she was menstruating: that she perform all the rituals except that she does not circumambulate the Kaaba."
"14574","(14574) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A menstruating woman may perform all rituals, except circumambulation of the Kaaba.

(Tirmidhi 945. Ahmad 6/137)"
"14575","(14575) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A menstruating woman performs all rituals. Except for circumambulating the Kaaba, and performing sa'y between Safa and Marwa."
"14576","(14576) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A menstruating woman performs the rituals. All of them, except for circumambulating the Kaaba and between As-Safa and Marwa."
"14577","(14577) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I said to Abu Al-Aaliyah: Should a menstruating woman read the Qur’an? He said: Do not recite the Qur’an, do not pray, do not circumambulate the Kaaba, or between al-Safa and al-Marwah. And he said: circumambulating between al-Safa. Marwa is equivalent to circumambulating the Kaaba."
"14578","(14578) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A menstruating woman may perform all rituals, except Tawaf"
"14579","(14579) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Munib, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: You perform all the rituals, except Tawaf of the Kaaba."
"14580","(14580) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: I heard him say: You stand according to your custom and make up for it. All rituals, except circumambulation of the House."
"14581","(14581) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Hani’, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali, He said: A menstruating woman may perform all rituals, except circumambulation of the Kaaba."
"14582","(14582) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, who said: My wife circumambulated and prayed two rak’ahs, then she menstruated before circumambulating between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, so I ordered her to circumambulate between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, but a woman heard me command her to do that, and she said: What a blessing she commanded her to do. She was your paternal aunt and paternal aunt, Aisha and Umm Salama, the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They say: If a woman circumambulates the Kaaba, then prays two rak’ahs, then menstruates, then she should circumambulate between Safa and Marwa."
"14583","(14583) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If she circumambulates At home, then she had her period before she started saa’i between Safa and Marwa, so she should saa’i between Safa and Marwa."
"14584","(14584) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a woman who circumambulated the Kaaba, then she menstruated? He said: Run between Safa and Marwa."
"14585","(14585) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, who said: Strive between Safa and Marwa."
"14586","(14586) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: Strive between Safa and Marwa."
"14587","(14587) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he came to the House on the Day of Sacrifice, he made one circumambulation, then he came to his place, and said, then he went to Mina and did not return to it. The house."
"14588","(14588) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; On the day of the visit there was no more than one circumambulation."
"14589","(14589) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like to circumambulate on the Day of Sacrifice for three days. Weeks"
"14590","(14590) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, who said: I performed a circumambulation with Sa’id bin Jubayr on the Day of Sacrifice. One"
"14591","(14591) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: I went out with Al-Hasan, and when the Day of Sacrifice came, we visited him. The House, so we circumambulated the House once, and ran between Safa and Marwa, then we returned to Minna."
"14592","(14592) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; He used to perform one circumambulation on the day of the visit."
"14593","(14593) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I and Al-Qasim visited the House at the end of the dawn prayer, and we performed one circumambulation when In the morning, then we returned to Minna."
"14594","(14594) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer at Arafat, then he prayed the afternoon prayer, meaning at Arafat, and he did not say the tasbih between them. Something"
"14595","(14595) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar; He combined Dhuhr and Asr at Arafat, then he stopped."
"14596","(14596) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya and Al-Aswad. They said: Abd Al-Aswad said: God: The two prayers cannot be combined except by custom, the noon and the afternoon prayers."
"14597","(14597) Ibn Numayr and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr, He said: From the Sunnah of Hajj, when he finishes his sermon, he descends and prays the noon and afternoon prayers together, then stands according to custom."
"14598","(14598) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: It is from the Sunnah to combine between them by knowledge."
"14599","(14599) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I prayed behind Salim, and the servants of God were with his knowledge. So they combined the two prayers, and did not recite the recitation out loud."
"14600","(14600) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He combines the noon and afternoon prayers. By knowledge"
"14601","(14601) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, who said: The imam delays the noon prayer. On the Day of Arafat, he delays it the most by any day of the year, and he accelerates the afternoon the most by any day of the year."
"14602","(14602) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: No one should spend the night behind me. Al-Aqaba at night in Mina during the days of Tashreeq."
"14603","(14603) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar had forbidden anyone from spending the night behind Al-Aqaba, and he ordered them to enter from there."
"14604","(14604) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He disliked that he should sleep in Mecca for any of his days."
"14605","(14605) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in having the beginning of the night in Mecca and the end of it in Mina. There is no harm in having the beginning of the night in Mina and the end of it in Mecca."
"14606","(14606) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka’b say: From the Sunnah When you visit the House, do not spend the night without making a mistake."
"14607","(14607) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Qalab, He said: Make the days of Mina with Mina."
"14608","(14608) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He said: No one will spend the night behind the Aqaba during the days of the Tashreeq."
"14609","(14609) Abu Bakr bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he spends the night before Al-Aqaba, he will leave for that. Blood"
"14610","(14610) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked about a man who spent a few nights in Mecca. ? He said: He gives a dirham or the like in charity."
"14611","(14611) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Najih told us. On the authority of Mujahid: He hated to stay the whole night without leaving."
"14612","(14612) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Bukair ibn Mismar, on the authority of Salim, who said: He gives a dirham in charity, meaning if he spends the night About me"
"14613","(14613) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to stay in Mecca for a few nights, so he gave permission. For his sake, for his sake.

(Bukhari 1745, Abu Dawud 1954)"
"14614","(14614) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: If you stone the Jamarat, spend the night wherever you want."
"14615","(14615) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Nafi’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, He said: There is no harm in a man spending a few nights in Mecca if he is in his country."
"14616","(14616) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca and may He be forgiven. (Bukhari 1846. Abu Dawud 2678)"
"14617","(14617) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Hawshab, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace When they enter ihram, they carry swords with them in their sacks."
"14618","(14618) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not hate to travel with swords in near it, and they are forbidden."
"14619","(14619) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; That his father used to enter the sanctuary with a sword."
"14620","(14620) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a muhrim wearing a sword if He was afraid"
"14621","(14621) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: No one shall enter Mecca with a weapon during Hajj, nor Omar"
"14622","(14622) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, who said: I think that I heard Qays bin Saad say: Ibn Omar said: A person in ihram does not carry weapons."
"14623","(14623) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: A person in ihram should not enter with a weapon."
"14624","(14624) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: I asked a servant of Ibn Umar about the death of Ibn Umar? He said: A man from the Levant struck him with a calamity, so Al-Hajjaj came in and said to him: If I knew who struck you, I would do it and I did it. He said: You injured me, you introduced the sacred weapon."
"14625","(14625) Abu Khaled narrated to us, not in Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abul Safar; He entered the sanctuary wearing a girded sword, so when he entered he removed it."
"14626","(14626) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Silt, on the authority of Uqba bin Saban, who said: I saw Uthman in Al-Abtah, and that Fustatah He was struck, and his sword was hanging from the tent."
"14627","(14627) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas and he came to him. A man, and he said: I have sacrificed my body, and I have led it astray on the way, so will that suffice for me? He said: If it is for a vow, or for expiation, then fulfill it in the house, then I do not think you will fulfill it, even if it is Voluntarily, I will suffice on your behalf. He said: I said: What about it, even if it were a sheep? He said: Yes."
"14628","(14628) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; Omar judged the rabbit unjustly."
"14629","(14629) Yahya bin Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: In the rabbit there is a handful of food, and what Without it"
"14630","(14630) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: In the rabbit there is tea."
"14631","(14631) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Aqeel narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Concerning the rabbit below The elderly"
"14632","(14632) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Omar, Othman, Zayd bin Thabit, Ibn Abbas, and Muawiyah said: In the ostriches there is a body."
"14633","(14633) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: In the ostrich’s body."
"14634","(14634) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In the ostriches there is a body."
"14635","(14635) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: There are many vultures in ostriches."
"14636","(14636) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is a body in the ostrich."
"14637","(14637) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In Al-Baqarah there is a cow."
"14638","(14638) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: If a person in ihram harms his cows The beast, there are mountains in it."
"14639","(14639) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, who said: In Al-Baqarah there are cows."
"14640","(14640) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In the donkey there is a body."
"14641","(14641) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: In the donkey. cows"
"14642","(14642) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That a man was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram, and his she-camel calfed him and he died, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him in his garment, and do not cover his head, and do not touch him with perfume. For, on the Day of Resurrection, God will resurrect him in a cloud. (Bukhari 1851, Muslim 99)"
"14643","(14643) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do not cover his head, for God will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection, reciting the Talbiyah. (Muslim 98. Abu Dawud 3233)"
"14644","(14644) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about whether a mahram in ihram should have his head covered when he dies. And if he is shrouded? He said: Ibn Umar covered it, and others revealed it."
"14645","(14645) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The head of the person in ihram will be hidden. If he dies"
"14646","(14646) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a person in ihram dies, it is lawful."
"14647","(14647) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Aamir, who said: If a person in ihram dies, his ihram is gone."
"14648","(14648) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If a person in ihram dies Your friend's ihram has gone."
"14649","(14649) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; She was asked about a person in ihram dying? She said: Do to him as you do to your dead."
"14650","(14650) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yasar, who said: I heard Ikrimah, and he was asked about the man. He dies while in ihram? He said: His ihram has gone, and he will be shrouded as a lawful person is shrouded."
"14651","(14651) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Cover your faces, and do not resemble the Jews. (Tabarani 11. Bayhaqi 393)"
"14652","(14652) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said regarding Muharram: He should cover his head, but not It will be revealed"
"14653","(14653) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not offer perfume to it."
"14654","(14654) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikayah, and Ata’; That Aisha bought a body and lost it, so she bought its place, then she found it, so she slaughtered them both, then she said: It was within the knowledge of God that He would slaughter them both. That is voluntary."
"14655","(14655) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Aisha slaughtered them all."
"14656","(14656) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ma’iz ibn Malik, or Malik ibn Ma’iz al-Thaqafi, who said: He led my father away from himself, his wife, and his daughter, and led them astray by this metaphor. When it was the Day of Sacrifice, he mentioned That is for Omar, so he said: Wait today and tomorrow and the day after, for the sacrifice is only during these three days, so if you find Then sacrifice them both, but if you do not find them, then buy two sacrifices on the third day, then sacrifice them and do not become permissible. unlawful until you slaughter them, or two other sacrificial animals. If you slaughter the two sacrificial animals that you bought and find The two men who are still astray, so slaughter them."
"14657","(14657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Aqeel bin Talha, on the authority of Abu al-Khasib al-Qaisi; He gave away a body on behalf of his mother and led her astray, so he bought another in her place, and imitated her, then?? He found the first one, so he asked Ibn Omar? He said: Kill them all."
"14658","(14658) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Talib al-Hajjam, and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: We will slaughter them all."
"14659","(14659) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; She brought two camels to her and she slaughtered them, so Ibn al-Zubayr gave her two camels and she slaughtered them, then she found The two camels, and she slaughtered them."
"14660","(14660) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ali ibn Nafi’, who said: I drove a body and lost it, so I bought another. So I slaughtered it, then I found the first one, so I asked Urwa bin Al-Zubair? He said: Slaughter them both, and I asked Ikrimah? He said: A camel from your camel."
"14661","(14661) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Sacrifice the first one."
"14662","(14662) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm, He said: I asked Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb about him? He said: Kill them all."
"14663","(14663) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Kathir ibn Shandhir, on the authority of Ata, who said: If it is the first Voluntarily, he sacrifices them both, and if it is obligatory, he can do whatever he wants with the other."
"14664","(14664) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They said about a man who voluntarily misled his own animal and bought another one. They said: If he imitated the one who bought it, we will burn them, but if he did not He can imitate her, sell her if he wishes."
"14665","(14665) Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever dies and has not performed the Hajj of Islam, he will not be prevented by a lingering illness, an apparent pilgrimage, or a ruler. He is unjust, so let him die under any circumstances he wishes, whether he is a Jew or a Christian. (Darimi 1785, Bayhaqi 334)"
"14666","(14666) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Aswad said to a wealthy man among them: If You died and did not perform Hajj, I did not pray for you."
"14667","(14667) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mujahid bin Rumi, and he was trustworthy. He said: I asked Sa`id bin Jubayr, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, and Abdullah bin Maqil on the authority of a man who died and did not perform Hajj, and he was well off? Sa`id said: Hell, Hell. Ibn Maqil said: He died disobeying God, and Ibn Abi Layla said: I hope that he will perform Hajj on his behalf. His guardian"
"14668","(14668) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’alla, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If I had a well-off neighbor Then he died and did not perform Hajj, and I did not pray for him."
"14669","(14669) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwair, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever dies while being well-off does not He will perform Hajj. He will come on the Day of Resurrection and before his eyes it will be written: An infidel."
"14670","(14670) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Adiy ibn Adiyy, on the authority of his father, he said: Umar ibn Al-Khattab: Whoever dies while being wealthy and does not perform Hajj, let him die under any circumstances he wishes, whether he is a Jew or a Christian."
"14671","(14671) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Adiy ibn Adiy, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Azm, on the authority of About Omar; In the same way"
"14672","(14672) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I saw Ibn Al-Zubayr hastening to circumambulate."
"14673","(14673) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul-Aziz running away. In Tawaf."
"14674","(14674) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Amr bin Maymun circumambulating the Kaaba. He accelerates to the point of almost running, or becomes intense."
"14675","(14675) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I circumambulated the Kaaba with him, and he was He walks slowly, little by little, and does not crowd the stone."
"14676","(14676) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr said to us while we were circumambulating the Kaaba: O young people. Be widowed, hurry."
"14677","(14677) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus, who said: We sat with Ibn Umar to watch how he was circling, and we saw him. Saying thus, he clenched his fingers as he became stronger."
"14678","(14678) Jarir and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, who said: Abu Qatada was with a group of people in ihram, and Abu Qatada was in a place, and his companions saw a wild donkey, so they did not even call it to prayer. He saw it, so he snatched a whip from some of them and struck him. They ate and carried some of it, and they met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they asked him about him? He said: Did any of you point to it? They said: No, he said: So eat. (Bukhari 1821. Muslim 63)"
"14679","(14679) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Muadh bin Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, said: We were with Talha bin Ubaid Allah during Hajj while we were in ihram. He said: Then a bird was given to us. Talhah was asleep. He said: Some of us ate it, and some of us were hesitant and did not eat it. When Talhah woke up, they mentioned that to him. He said: The one who ate it agreed and said: We ate it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 65 Ahmad 1/162)"
"14680","(14680) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Omar ibn al-Khattab saw nothing wrong with the meat of birds if he hunted for someone else, meaning while in ihram."
"14681","(14681) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Salim, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: When I came from Bahrain A group of people from Iraq met me and asked me about what is permissible to catch game and eat what is forbidden? So I issued a fatwa to them about eating it, so I came to Omar and asked him about that? He said: If I had given them a fatwa other than that, I would never have given a fatwa to anyone."
"14682","(14682) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam used to provide food for the beast while he was in ihram."
"14683","(14683) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Because they did not see any harm in a forbidden person eating what he caught that was lawful, if he did not catch it for his own sake, or With his god"
"14684","(14684) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad bin Ayadh, he said: Ibn Masoud was asked About a people who were in ihram, they met a people who had permissible game meat with them, so they either sold it to them, or fed them to them? He said: No problem."
"14685","(14685) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh bin Khalid, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, who said: A man said: We bought a A donkey, and we are in a state of ihram from a lawful people. He said: So we passed by Abu Dharr, and we asked him? He said: I do not see you being immoral, there is nothing wrong with that."
"14686","(14686) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, who said: I gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the cows, or the two paws of a wild donkey, while he was in ihram. He said: He responded to him and said: We have no right to respond to you, but we are inviolable. (Bukhari 1825. Muslim 50)"
"14687","(14687) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Saab bin Juthama presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a wild donkey while he was in ihram, and he returned it to him and said: Had we not been in ihram, we would have accepted it from you. (Muslim 54. Ahmad 1/280)"
"14688","(14688) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He disliked fresh game and fresh game for a mahram."
"14689","(14689) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Saab bin Juthama gave the gift. A zebra was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Return it to him, for we are in ihram."
"14690","(14690) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus; He used to forbid the forbidden from eating game or anything else."
"14691","(14691) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’ath’i; He disliked eating it for a person in ihram, and he recited: {And forbidden to you is the game of land as long as you remain in ihram}"
"14692","(14692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, he said: She said: O son of my sister, These are only nights, so if something stirs in your heart, let it go."
"14693","(14693) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is ambiguous."
"14694","(14694) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Subayh, on the authority of Ali; He hated it"
"14695","(14695) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith; Othman was given a partridge as a gift while he was on one of his pilgrimages while he was in ihram, so he ordered it to be cooked, and it was made into porridge. So it was brought in a drought while we were in ihram, and they all ate it except Ali."
"14696","(14696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about him? He said: There has been disagreement about it, but do not eat from it, it is more beloved to me."
"14697","(14697) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you are able not to come near your wife while you are forbidden."
"14698","(14698) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He was ordering her to isolate herself very much."
"14699","(14699) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, who said: I asked Nafi’ about him? He said: There is no harm in it."
"14700","(14700) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man carrying his wife while he is in a state of ihram. He said: Carry her and fear God."
"14701","(14701) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; In the same way"
"14702","(14702) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him carrying her, as long as she is not touched"
"14703","(14703) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram carrying His wife, unless his skin sticks to hers."
"14704","(14704) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Marwan bin Al-Hakam asked Ibn Abbas while we were in a valley. Al-Azraq, and he said: The hunt is hunted by the ihram, and he does not find any equal blessings for it? Ibn Abbas said: Its price will be given to Mecca."
"14705","(14705) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a person in ihram catches some game that was not in it, As a gift, give its price in charity."
"14706","(14706) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Unless he reaches a sacrifice, then food. He feeds him"
"14707","(14707) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: He imitated this verse while it was Muharram. He said:

And they walked with us whispering. If you give charity to birds, you will be blessed with rain.

 He said: He was told: You say this while you are in ihram, so he said: Indecency is only what women are confronted with while they are in ihram."
"14708","(14708) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus; He disliked the inscription for a muhrim. I said: What is the inflection? He said: To say: If you had permitted it, I would have struck you."
"14709","(14709) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked the Arabization of the ihram."
"14710","(14710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Maqil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair; He disliked the Arabization of the ihram."
"14711","(14711) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubair, on the authority of Tawus; That Abdullah bin Al-Zubair said: Beware of women, for decency is a form of obscenity. Tawoos said: So I informed Ibn Abbas about that. He said: Ibn al-Zubayr spoke the truth."
"14712","(14712) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no temporary supplication on Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, so pray Whatever you want"
"14713","(14713) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We did not hear any supplications for Safa and Marwa. Temporarily"
"14714","(14714) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: There is no temporary supplication upon them, so pray as you wish. Ask whatever you want."
"14715","(14715) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh ibn al-Ala’, who said: I heard Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzoumi saying: No. I know about Al-Safa and Al-Marwah a temporary supplication."
"14716","(14716) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Wahb ibn Al-Ajda’; He heard Omar say: He begins with Safa and faces the House, then he says “Allahu Akbar” seven times, between each Two forms of arrogance, praise be to God and blessings be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a question to oneself, and on the narration, for example That"
"14717","(14717) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he ascended the Safa, he would face the House, then say “Allahu Akbar” three times, then say: There is no god but Allah, alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. He raises his voice with it, then he supplicates a little, then he does it. That is according to the narration, until he does that seven times, so the takbeer is twenty-one, so what It is almost empty to the point that it becomes difficult for us, and we are young."
"14718","(14718) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, because he used to say: A man will stand on Safa and Al-Marwah as much as he recites Surahs of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"14719","(14719) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Al-Hakam said to Ibrahim: I saw Abu Bakr ibn Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith recites Al-Safa as much as a man recites twenty and a hundred verses. He said: Indeed, he is a jurist."
"14720","(14720) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, started with As-Safa, then proceeded to the top, declared God alone and glorified Him, and said: There is no god but God alone. Your partner is His, to Him is the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. There is no god but Allah alone. He has fulfilled His promise. And he supported his servant, and defeated the parties alone, then he called in between that, and said like that three times, then he descended to Al-Marwah until his feet reached the bottom of the valley, until when we ascended, he walked until he reached Al-Marwah, so he did so. Al-Marwah as he did on Al-Safa."
"14721","(14721) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: Whoever braids, twists, or crimps Let him shave, and Ibn Abbas said: He did not intend."
"14722","(14722) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, who said: I went out with my aunt Maimunah, and I was in trouble. I covered my head with honey or glue, and it spread. It was difficult for me while I was in ihram, so I asked her? She said: Dip your head in water several times."
"14723","(14723) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever wears hair, or curls it, or braids it. Quickly, it is obligatory for him to shave."
"14724","(14724) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qais, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, who said: Whoever wears a hair, or plaits it, Or let him shave."
"14725","(14725) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I asked about him, and they claimed that he was Abu Al-Muhallab. He said: Whoever has long hair or braids, it is obligatory for him to shave."
"14726","(14726) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was said: He who wears a hair, or plaits it. Let him shave."
"14727","(14727) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said: I put clay on my head before I entered ihram, and I met Ibn Al-Zubair, and he said: As for Omar, he used to see the earrings on those who wore hair, but as for me, I only see what you intended."
"14728","(14728) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; In a state of ihram, if he needs a shirt to wear, or to shave his head, or something like that that a state of ihram does not need, Of what it is not appropriate for us to do. He said: If he does it all together, there is a single blood liability for him, and if he does it separately, then every one of That is blood."
"14729","(14729) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: If he combines all of that in an hour, then one blood is due on him. And if there is a difference between the two, then there is blood for each of them."
"14730","(14730) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Al-Qasim performing voluntary prayers between the noon and afternoon prayers according to his custom. And I saw Salim doing nothing."
"14731","(14731) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He did not volunteer between them."
"14732","(14732) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He greeted the noon and afternoon prayers with his custom, and did not say the tasbih between them."
"14733","(14733) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Pray between the noon and afternoon prayers with your knowledge, if you wish."
"14734","(14734) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever prays the two prayers according to his will, has not performed voluntary prayers. Between them."
"14735","(14735) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the imam enables you to do voluntary prayers between them, So he volunteered."
"14736","(14736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, who said: I saw Ibn Umar not performing voluntary prayers between noon and afternoon prayers. With your knowledge, and I saw Al-Qasim volunteering."
"14737","(14737) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He used to perform voluntary prayers between noon and afternoon according to his custom."
"14738","(14738) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, who said: I asked Anas bin Malik about Muharram. Will he slaughter? He said: Yes."
"14739","(14739) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The person in ihram slaughters everything, except game."
"14740","(14740) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim. He said: I asked Ata’, and they said: There is no harm in a person in ihram slaughtering something that is not game."
"14741","(14741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I asked him about the sacrifice in Muharram? He did not see any harm in it. He said: And the judge did not see any harm in it."
"14742","(14742) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The sacrifice of a muhrim is dead."
"14743","(14743) Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The sacrifice of a muhrim is like a dead body, it cannot be eaten."
"14744","(14744) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abu Ma’iz, who said: She came A woman went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, I have undergone menstruation. He said: Leave the prayer in your days. These are your days, then wash yourself, fill yourself with a blanket, circumambulate the Kaaba and pray."
"14745","(14745) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Regarding the woman who is in need of menstruation, he said: “Wait, let her wash herself and clean herself with her effort, and put on a clean garment, then circumambulate the Kaaba.”"
"14746","(14746) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, the client of Banu Hashim, who said: A woman came to me. To Ibn Abbas, and she said: Should the woman undergoing menstrual bleeding circumambulate the Kaaba? He said: She will spend the days of her reading, then she will wash and circumambulate the Kaaba. He said: She said: Will you enter the Kaaba? He said: So he said: Go in and mobilize yourself, and go in."
"14747","(14747) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I asked him: Should I pray? The one who needs menstruation? He said: Yes, and you may perform Hajj to the Kaaba even if water is asked on your heels."
"14748","(14748) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan; They both said: You perform the rituals."
"14749","(14749) Hammad bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The woman who is experiencing istihaadah circumambulates the Kaaba. And between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"14750","(14750) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of a woman from the people of Mecca, on the authority of Aisha; She walked around with me seeking water."
"14751","(14751) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’; He said: The woman undergoing menstruation sits in the same way she used to sit, then she gets up, takes a bath, and circumambulates the Kaaba. And you flee."
"14752","(14752) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: I said to Nafi’: When did Ibn Umar go? He said: His Messenger is with the Imam, and when he departs, he departs, hastens, or delays. He said: He would not depart until he had circumambulated seven times, and he would He likes not to pray the noon prayer without making a prayer. He said: The prince delayed his prayer and prayed without a prayer."
"14753","(14753) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: I saw a human being riding a donkey. I was going to Manna on the Day of Tarwiyah, and I said to him: Where did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the afternoon prayer on this? Today? He said: Look where your leaders pray and pray."
"14754","(14754) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He prays the noon prayer on the Day of Tarwiyah in Mecca, then He goes to Mina and spends the night there."
"14755","(14755) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Mina and prayed the noon and afternoon prayers there, And the sunset, the evening, and the morning."
"14756","(14756) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The souls go to Mina when The sun has set, so let the Imam depart."
"14757","(14757) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer. On the Day of Tarwiyah with Mina."
"14758","(14758) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Aisha used to stay in Mecca. The night of Arafah, the evening of the Day of Tarwiyah, the whole night."
"14759","(14759) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I prayed the evening prayer with him in Mecca the night before. The narration"
"14760","(14760) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: I heard Ibn Al-Zubayr saying: Indeed, from the Sunnah Hajj, the imam prays the dawn and afternoon prayers, and the sunset, evening and dawn prayers, then he goes in the morning."
"14761","(14761) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ata’ said: Whoever wishes may pray the noon prayer in Mecca, and whoever wishes may pray at noon. Why?"
"14762","(14762) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr on the day of the Tarwiyah. He prayed two rak'ahs in the Sacred Mosque, then he left Mecca walking until he came to a place, where he prayed the noon prayer. And the afternoon, and the sunset, and the evening, and the dawn."
"14763","(14763) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Lahiq bin Hamid, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer next to Ibn Omar, His mount was stopped, so when he looked at the sun at the top of the mountain, he mounted his mount, then went to Arafat tomorrow."
"14764","(14764) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Tell me who saw Ibn Abbas perform his magic spell."
"14765","(14765) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: Abraham, for he spent the night in Mina, until when the morning came and the veil of the sun rose, he walked until he came to his resting place from Arafah. (Ibn Khuzaymah 2803)"
"14766","(14766) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the dawn prayer, then stayed for a little while until the sun rose, then he walked."
"14767","(14767) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When you pray the dawn prayer, go to Arafat, and go down to the places where the people are."
"14768","(14768) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw the imams, the imams of the season. They will move towards Arafat in the morning at sunrise, and I do not see them moving there except as their Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did."
"14769","(14769) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I prayed Fajr with Al-Qasim in Minna, then he stayed for an hour, then he departed."
"14770","(14770) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, he said: No maniy comes out of it. To Arafat until he performs the morning prayer at Mina."
"14771","(14771) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar taking the stone in his hand and kissing his hand. He said: I have not abandoned it since I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do it. (Muslim 246 Bayhaqi 75)"
"14772","(14772) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar and Abu Hurairah when they received Al-Rukn, meaning the stone, they kissed their hands. He said: I said to Ata: And Ibn Abbas? He said: And Ibn Abbas, you thought a lot. He said: And Ata’ said: I would not wipe the corner unless I kissed my hand. He said: Amr bin Dinar said: He who wipes the corner and does not kiss his hand will be cursed."
"14773","(14773) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Murtaffa’, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr and Umar ibn Abd. Al-Aziz received the stone, and one of them kissed his hand, and the other wiped his face with it."
"14774","(14774) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: I did not see my father receiving the stone. Unless he kisses her hand."
"14775","(14775) Ibn Fudayl and Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr wiping the stone, then He kisses her hand."
"14776","(14776) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Mujahid and Sa’id bin Mighty and generous; When they receive the Yemeni pillar, they kiss their hands."
"14777","(14777) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Tariq, who said: I saw Ali bin Hussein adhering to the pillar. Yemeni."
"14778","(14778) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawus; Concerning a man who forgets the two rak’ahs required for the obligatory Tawaf, they said: If he prays a prayer after it, that is sufficient for him, and if he prays In the nearest part of the sanctuary and the farthest parts of it, and if he does not pray until he comes out of the sanctuary, he will shed blood."
"14779","(14779) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who circumambulated the Kaaba and forgot to pray the two rak’ahs until he went on, he said: He prays them when he remembers, not Something wrong with him."
"14780","(14780) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who forgot the two rak’ahs of tawaf, he said: He will perform them wherever he remembers them, as long as he does not cheat with women."
"14781","(14781) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Attab bin Ziyad bin Warqa’, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying to the barber: Convey the message of the throat to the two bones."
"14782","(14782) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say to the barber, when he shaved during Hajj and Umrah: Reach the two bones."
"14783","(14783) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say to the barber: Start with the right hand, and reach the two bones by shaving."
"14784","(14784) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Harith bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ali Al-Azdi, he said: Ibn Umar slaughtered and shaved. He said: I heard him say to the barber: Tell the two bones. He said: So I said to Ata’: I heard him say to the barber: Tell the two greats? He said: I heard them mentioning it, but I did not hear it from proven sources."
"14785","(14785) Junaid Al-Hajjam narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhtar bin Munih, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: Report to the great ones."
"14786","(14786) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Sunnah is to reach the throat to the bones."
"14787","(14787) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas; He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying this to the barber, and pointing with his hand to the right side. (Muslim 325. Tirmidhi 912)"
"14788","(14788) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say to the barber: Start with the right hand."
"14789","(14789) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: The man who fell short of Nafi’ told me Ibn Alqamah in his emirate, he said: So he said to me: Start with the left part. He said: I said: I fell short of Ibn Abbas. He said: Start. With the right hand, he said: Go ahead with what you were commanded to do."
"14790","(14790) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he stones the Jamarat when the sun has passed the zenith. (Tirmidhi 898, Ahmad 1/248)"
"14791","(14791) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to stone the stones when the sun rose."
"14792","(14792) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw Omar going out when When the sun passed, he stoned the Jamaraat."
"14793","(14793) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: He throws stones. The pebbles when the sun rises."
"14794","(14794) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr and Ubaid ibn Amir throws stones at the stones after the sun has set."
"14795","(14795) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiyah, who said: I looked at Ibn Abbas when he shot her. The afternoon before it passes."
"14796","(14796) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr waiting for the sun to noon. The sun, then he stones the Jamaraat."
"14797","(14797) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail: He said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr, and a peacock throwing two stones. The pebbles are performed at noon, and they prolong the qiyaam."
"14798","(14798) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like him"
"14799","(14799) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata’ saying: Do not stone the Jamarat until the sun has set. So I went back to him about that, and he said that."
"14800","(14800) Abdullah bin Idris and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned Jamarat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice as a sacrifice, and after that, when the sun had passed, he sacrificed.

(Muslim 314, Abu Dawud 511)"
"14801","(14801) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; The same, but he did not raise it."
"14802","(14802) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, or on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us One night, we set out on the Humrat of Ughilami of Banu Abdul Muttalib, and he started smearing our thighs and saying: Tell me, do not throw stones. The Jamarat until the sun rises, and I do not think anyone will stone it until the sun rises. And Ibn Abbas used to say: Whoever spends more than He is stripped, so there is no Hajj for him."
"14803","(14803) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not stone Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Judgment. Sacrifice, until the sun rises."
"14804","(14804) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Abu Ja’far stone the Jamarat. Before sunrise, Ata’, Tawoos, Mujahid, Al-Nakha’i, Aamir, and Sa’id bin Jubayr were throwing stones at They are coming, what a courier they are coming, they see no harm in it."
"14805","(14805) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in a man stoning Jamarat al-Aqaba before the sun rose."
"14806","(14806) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I wish I were I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, for permission, just as Suda had asked for permission to come from the place at night and throw stones at night. Before the people came, he gave her permission, but she was a depressed and heavy woman. (Bukhari 1480, Muslim 2951, Ahmad 6/98)"
"14807","(14807) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abdullah, he said: Ibn Omar would send his boys on the night of Muzdalifah, and they would perform the Fajr prayer at Mina, and stone the Jamarat before the people came."
"14808","(14808) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while he was in ihram. (Bukhari 1835, Abu Dawud 1831)"
"14809","(14809) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawi, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cupped while he was in ihram, as a result of a garment he had. (Abu Dawud 1831)"
"14810","(14810) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Muqisim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping while he was in ihram. (Abu Dawud 2365. Ahmad 1/215)"
"14811","(14811) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, who said: It was said to Ata’: Should a person in ihram use cupping? He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did that, but he did not shave his hair."
"14812","(14812) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, He said: The person in ihram should be cupped, but he should not shave his hair."
"14813","(14813) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Hanzali, who said: Tawoos was asked: Should a person in ihram use cupping? He said: Yes, if it is pain."
"14814","(14814) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The person in ihram should use cupping, but he should not use cupping. The fasting person"
"14815","(14815) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping while he was in ihram. (Abu Dawud 1833. Ahmad 3/267)"
"14816","(14816) Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Abi Alqamiya, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn In our time; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping while he was in ihram. (Muslim 88)"
"14817","(14817) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was cupped while in ihram, over his hair, in a place called Lahya al-Jamal."
"14818","(14818) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They disliked that the person in ihram should use cupping."
"14819","(14819) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in a person in ihram smelling something. basil"
"14820","(14820) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He saw no harm in it."
"14821","(14821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram smelling basil."
"14822","(14822) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of someone who saw with Abdullah bin Amer was going to Arafat for Hajj, while he was in Muharram."
"14823","(14823) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid said: There is no harm in a person in ihram smelling basil."
"14824","(14824) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to smell the itkhira."
"14825","(14825) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no problem. That the pilgrim in ihram should smell the perfume of the earth’s plants and the dung of the deer."
"14826","(14826) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, and Ata`, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram smelling something. The goodness of the earth’s plants."
"14827","(14827) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; It was disliked for a person in ihram to smell basil."
"14828","(14828) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, who said: I asked Jabir: Who should smell the muhrim? Basil and perfume? He said: No."
"14829","(14829) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: The person in ihram should not smell wormwood or qisum."
"14830","(14830) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If a person in ihram smells basil, or... He touched perfume and it shed blood."
"14831","(14831) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In perfume there is a ransom, and in the reward game."
"14832","(14832) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a person in ihram smells perfume, he disbelieves."
"14833","(14833) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the forbidden person is placed on something It is a good oil, so expiation is required."
"14834","(14834) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: There is no harm in a person in ihram being treated with henna. He hated that he should wear his khatib with it."
"14835","(14835) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in seeking medical treatment. The ihram with henna."
"14836","(14836) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hammad, who said: A person in ihram should not dye his hair with henna, nor He performs ablution with Desbasan."
"14837","(14837) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is from the Sunnah not to He performs the Hajj, except during the months of the Hajj."
"14838","(14838) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He does not enter into ihram for Hajj, except During the months of Hajj."
"14839","(14839) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: He does not enter ihram for Hajj, except during the months of Hajj."
"14840","(14840) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, who said: A man from the people of Khurasan came, having entered ihram for Hajj in other months. Hajj, so Ataa said to him: Make it a lifetime, for there is no Hajj for you, for God Almighty says: {Hajj is known for months. Then whoever makes Hajj obligatory therein}"
"14841","(14841) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man came to perform Hajj during other than the months of Hajj. So Ata ordered him to make her a lifetime."
"14842","(14842) Sharik and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who qualified for Hajj in other than the months of Hajj, Sharik said: He will go on, and Hushaym said: He will commit to it."
"14843","(14843) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Dalani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: He is permissible, or he declares his life as permissible."
"14844","(14844) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ibn Abi Na’am used to perform Hajj in other than The months of Hajj, and Amr ibn Maymun said: If this had happened to the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, they would have stoned him."
"14845","(14845) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub; Abu Al-Hakam Al-Bajli used to perform Hajj during other months of Hajj. He said: Ikrimah met him and said: You are a man. Bad"
"14846","(14846) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Because they did not see anything wrong with a man drinking while circumambulating the Kaaba."
"14847","(14847) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the Al-Wada’ family, who said : The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked for something to drink while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, and a man said: Shall we not give you something to drink that we make? So he brought him a vessel containing raisin wine, and he said: Didn't you give him a vessel or offer him a stick? Then he drank from it and frowned, then he called for water and poured it into it and drank? And he gave his companions drink."
"14848","(14848) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in drinking during Tawaf."
"14849","(14849) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Masoud; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked for water while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, and he was brought with some wine from the drinker’s wine. So he drank it."
"14850","(14850) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata, who said: If something forbidden is made lawful, He caught a hunt and did not catch it, so let him ask God for forgiveness."
"14851","(14851) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"14852","(14852) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Omar said: Let the last of your covenant be with the House. And let your last pledge be from the House with stone."
"14853","(14853) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I said to Abraham: By what other thing would it be? Are you from home? He said: He said: With the stone."
"14854","(14854) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They used to like, when they said goodbye, to It will be their last covenant with stone."
"14855","(14855) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: If a person in ihram is forced to wear socks, He pierced their backs and left them as long as their feet could hold."
"14856","(14856) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a person in ihram is forced to wear socks, he should tear them off and leave them alone. In them he decrees the partnership, and He cuts them both off before Ka`bah."
"14857","(14857) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Nafi’ said: He cuts off the socks below the waist. The Kaabain"
"14858","(14858) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He should lighten his shoes if he does not find two sandals. He said: I said: Are they broken? He said: God does not like corruption."
"14859","(14859) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was permitting the ihram to wear socks, not closed."
"14860","(14860) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he does not find sandals, he should wear the socks lower than the ankles. (Bukhari 5794, Abu Dawud 1821)"
"14861","(14861) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He saw no harm in three divorced women and those whose husbands had died performing Hajj during their waiting period."
"14862","(14862) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Al-Qasim (H) and on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ata’; Aisha performed Umm Kulthum’s Hajj during her waiting period."
"14863","(14863) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in performing Hajj in her waiting period."
"14864","(14864) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib al-Mu’allim, who said: I asked Ata’ about a woman who has been divorced three times, and a man who died. About her, do you have to perform Hajj during her waiting period? He said: Yes, Habib said: Al-Hasan used to say that."
"14865","(14865) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Omar brought back his women who were performing Hajj, or those performing Umrah, who had gone out in their Iddah."
"14866","(14866) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Miqdam, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The one who died from her, A woman who has been divorced for three days must not perform Hajj, do Umrah, or wear any clothing."
"14867","(14867) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hamid al-Araj, on the authority of Mujahid; Omar and Othman returned women as Hajj pilgrims and Umrah performers, to the point that they performed the ‘iddah in their homes."
"14868","(14868) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a boy who caught a pigeon from the sanctuary and said: Sacrifice a sheep on behalf of your son."
"14869","(14869) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of his father, who said: We came as young men with Hafs bin Asim, we took a chick in Mecca in our house, and we played and played with it until we killed it, and his wife Aisha said to it: His son Muti’ bin Al-Aswad ordered a ram to be slaughtered and he gave it as charity."
"14870","(14870) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: Some of the Banu Urwa tampered with a young Meccan pigeon. So my father ordered a sheep, which was slaughtered and then given in charity."
"14871","(14871) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he catches some game, meaning a boy, He was the one with whom Hajj was performed."
"14872","(14872) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: {And the body We have made for you as part of rituals. Allah} What is the body? He said: The camels and the cows."
"14873","(14873) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of someone who heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: camels and cows."
"14874","(14874) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The body is not formed except by Camels"
"14875","(14875) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad said: The sheep will never be more than your women. And the cow is part of the body."
"14876","(14876) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, who said: Ata’ and the ruling differed, so Ata’ said: Of camels and cows, and the ruling said: It is of camels."
"14877","(14877) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yaqoub, on the authority of his father, who said: A living man died. He commanded that his body be slaughtered, so I asked Ibn Abbas about cows? He said: It is sufficient. He said: I said: Which people are you from? He said: I said: From Banu Rabah. He said: And I am from Banu Rabah al-Baqar? The cows are for Azd, and for Abd al-Qais."
"14878","(14878) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; He was circumambulating with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: How much do you count? Then he said: I only asked you to be careful."
"14879","(14879) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Dirham, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, and he was asked about saa’i between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa? Ibn Umar said to the questioner: Open with As-Safa and conclude with Al-Marwah. If you fear that you will not be counted, then take stones with you, or pebbles, throw one into al-Safa and another into al-Marwah."
"14880","(14880) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr; Sa`id bin Jubayr saw a woman walking around with pebbles in her hand, counting the circumambulation, so he hit her hands."
"14881","(14881) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: We used to circumambulate while upon us Our rings, with them we protect the seven days."
"14882","(14882) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Habiba, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A woman should not raise her voice when reciting the Talbiyah."
"14883","(14883) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"14884","(14884) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A woman does not dare to recite the Talbiyah."
"14885","(14885) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: He came out Mu'awiyah was on his way to the night of the army, and he heard the sound of your talbiyah, and he said: Who is this? They said: Aisha, she performed Umrah from Tan'im. This was mentioned to Aisha, and she said: If he had asked me, I would have told him."
"14886","(14886) Omar told us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Issa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: Women do not have to raise their hair. Their voices are called Talbiyah."
"14887","(14887) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdul Malik, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Nawfal, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b was asked: Should a person in ihram fasten a lace? He said: No."
"14888","(14888) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, he said: I heard his leaders narrating on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr; Concerning the buttoned tunic of the Muhrim, he said: He takes off his buttons."
"14889","(14889) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr was asked about the tongue. What should a person in ihram wear? He said: Do not wear it on yourself, and there is no harm in wearing a long hair."
"14890","(14890) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, who said: Ali Sa`id bin Jubayr saw a tongue, as if it was in it. I removed the brocade buttons, and he said: Why did you remove them? So I said to him: My friends said to me: Do you wear this while you are in ihram? So he said: What harm will it do to you?"
"14891","(14891) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in the ihram wearing a tongue unless he visited him on his behalf."
"14892","(14892) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Saeed; Indeed, Al-Hasan saw no harm in it."
"14893","(14893) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; He used to wear ihram while wearing a brocade, and he did not wear it over himself."
"14894","(14894) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Regarding the person in ihram who wears a talisman, he said: He wears it, but does not button it over him."
"14895","(14895) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father; That Saeed bin Jubayr used to wear ihram in a tanned coat, and that my father used to do it."
"14896","(14896) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He is put into ihram in a turban, but he does not visit it. Aliyah"
"14897","(14897) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in entering into ihram for it, but there is no harm in He visits her."
"14898","(14898) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Mecca. It is a sanctuary that God Almighty has made sacred. It is not permissible to sell its quarters or rent its houses."
"14899","(14899) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not permissible to rent houses in Mecca."
"14900","(14900) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated the rent of houses in Mecca."
"14901","(14901) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Whoever eats any of the rent of Mecca, it is He eats fire."
"14902","(14902) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I read the book of Omar bin Abdul Aziz to the people. In Mecca, he forbade them from renting the houses and houses of Mecca."
"14903","(14903) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: Those who eat the wages of the houses of Mecca are only eating fire into their bellies."
"14904","(14904) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Umar used to prevent the people of Mecca from making doors, until the pilgrim descends in the courtyards of the hall."
"14905","(14905) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The houses in Mecca did not have doors. The people of Egypt and the people of Iraq bring their newly created rituals and enter the homes of Mecca."
"14906","(14906) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujair, who said: I had a house in Mecca. So I hated it, so I asked Tawoos? So he ordered me to eat it."
"14907","(14907) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, he said: I was told by someone who heard Mujahid say: I see nothing wrong with renting houses in Mecca, unless a man is renting out houses and makes a profit."
"14908","(14908) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, who said: Uthman said: The four In Mecca, our children will live there, and those they love will live there."
"14909","(14909) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, Ata’, and Tawoos, who said: They hated that They sell something from the quarter of Mecca."
"14910","(14910) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not permissible to sell a quarter of it."
"14911","(14911) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who narrated it, saying: It is not permissible to sell a quarter of it."
"14912","(14912) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Alqamah bin Nadlah said: It was a quarter of Mecca in the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the time of Abu Bakr. Omar is called Al-Sawaib, whoever needs accommodation, and whoever is self-sufficient will be provided with accommodation. (Ibn Majah 3107)"
"14913","(14913) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah in the year of the conquest of the scarab, and when he completed his Umrah, he appointed Abu Bakr as the successor. Mecca, and commanded him to teach the people the rituals, and to announce to the people: Whoever performs Hajj in the year is safe, and should not perform Hajj after the year. A polytheist, and no one should circumambulate the Kaaba naked."
"14914","(14914) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came A Bedouin went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu Abdul Muttalib, and he said: And upon you, He said: I am a man from your maternal uncles from Banu Saad bin Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their envoy, and I am asking you. Then I asked you, and I appealed to you, and I continued to appeal to you. He said: Take it on your behalf, brother of Banu Sa’d. He said: So, we found in your book, and your messengers commanded us to perform Hajj to the Ancient House, so I adjure you. Did he command you to do that? He said: Yes.

(Darimi 651 Bayhaqi 4)"
"14915","(14915) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, he said: We returned to Medina, So we came to Abdullah bin Omar, and he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a well-dressed, good-natured man came to him. The wind, a beautiful face, and he said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: And upon you. He said: O Messenger of God, shall I come closer to you? He said: Come closer, so we came closer to you, so we said: We have never seen a man more beautifully dressed, nor more fragrant, nor more fragrant than today. He had the most beautiful face, and there was no greater reverence for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: O Messenger of God, shall I come closer to you? He said: Yes, so we came closer to you, so we said the same as we said, then the third said to him: Am I closer to you, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes, until he pressed his knees to the knees of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger, what is Islam? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You establish prayer, pay zakat, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, and bathe for The janaba, he said: You are right, so we said: We have never seen a man like today, and by God, it is as if he was teaching the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 1/53)"
"14916","(14916) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, should I start with Al-Safa before Al-Marwa, or with Al-Marwa before Al-Marwa? Or should I pray before I circumambulate, or should I circumambulate before I pray? Or should I slaughter before I shave, or should I shave before I slaughter? Ibn Abbas said: Take that from the beginning of the Qur’an, for it is more worthy of being preserved. God Almighty said: (Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwa are from The rituals of God) So Safa is before Marwah, and God Blessed and Most High said: (And do not shave your heads until the sacrifice reaches its place.) He said: By slaughtering before shaving, and he said: (Purify My House for those who circumambulate, those who seclude themselves, and those who kneel and prostrate), so tawaaf is before prayer."
"14917","(14917) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Yathai, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with four things when the Innocence was revealed: that no naked people should circumambulate the Kaaba, and that A polytheist approaches the mosque after this year of theirs, and whoever had a covenant between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace It will last forever, and only a Muslim soul will enter Paradise. (Ahmad 1/79 Hakim 178)"
"14918","(14918) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, who said: Al-Dahhak dictated to me the rituals of Hajj."
"14919","(14919) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, who said: Al-Dahhak dictated to me the rituals of Hajj."
"14920","(14920) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gabriel came to Abraham, peace be upon them, and he took him to Manna, so he prayed. He performed all the prayers with it, then he prayed the dawn prayer with it, then in the morning with it until Arafah, and he camped with it wherever the people camp, then he prayed with it. He performed all the two prayers, then he performed the prayer, and even if it was the haste of what a person prays Maghrib, he made up for it, so he performed it. All together, he led both prayers with it, then spent the night with it, and even if it was the fastest that any of the people prayed the dawn prayer, he prayed with it. Then he stood until it was as if he was the slowest of any of the people to pray the dawn prayer, and he carried it to Mina, then stoned the Jamarat, then He slaughtered and shaved, then he uttered it, then God Almighty later revealed to his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {To follow his creed. Ibrahim Hanif}"
"14921","(14921) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Abu Majliz; In the words of God Almighty: {And when Abraham raised the foundations of the House, and Ishmael} He said: When he had finished the House, Gabriel came to him. peace be upon him, so he showed him the circumambulation of the Kaaba, and I think he said: And as-Safa and al-Marwah. Then they set off for Al-Aqabah, and he showed them what Satan, he said: Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, took seven pebbles, and gave Abraham, peace be upon him, seven pebbles, and he threw it. And he said “Allahu Akbar” and said to Ibrahim: “Throw and say “Allahu Akbar.” He said: So they threw and said “Allahu Akbar” with every throw they threw, until Satan escaped, then they set off. To the middle burning coal, and Satan approached them, so Gabriel, peace be upon him, took seven pebbles and gave it to Abraham. He, peace be upon him, picked up seven pebbles. He threw them and said “Allahu Akbar” with each throwing until Satan fled. Then they came to the burning coal, he said: Then Satan appeared to them, he said: Then Gabriel, peace be upon him, took seven pebbles. And he gave Abraham, peace be upon him, seven pebbles, and said: Throw and say “Allahu Akbar.” So he threw and said “Allahu Akbar” with every throw he made, until he failed. Satan Then he brought him to Minna and said: Here the people are shaving their heads. Then he brought him to Minna and said: Here the people will gather. Prayer, then he brought him to Arafat and said: Did you know? He said: Yes, he said: Hence it was named Arafat."
"14922","(14922) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Musa; In the Almighty’s saying: {And whoever honors the rituals of God, it is from the strengthening of hearts.} He said: Standing according to God’s rituals is one of the rituals of God. And with a combination of the rituals of God, and the pebbles are among the rituals of God, and the body is among the rituals of God, and the throat is among the rituals of God, so who will venerate them? For it is the strengthening of hearts. He said: And in the Almighty’s saying: {In it there are benefits for you until an appointed time}. He said: In every place there are benefits, until that time. Leave from it to another place, for the specified term: exit from it to another place. {Then its place is to the Ancient House} He said. The place for all of these rituals is circumambulation of the House."
"14923","(14923) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {And take the place of Abraham as a place of prayer.} He said: This is the entire Hajj."
"14924","(14924) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, who said: He was with Ibn Umar, and when the The sun commanded his mount to set off, and he set off from Mina and set off. He said: If it had been, we would have admired and regretted it, a man who was He would talk to you about women and make you laugh. He said: When he prayed the afternoon prayer, he stood with his custom, and began to raise his hand, or he said: He extended, he said. : And I do not know whether he might have said: without my permission, and started saying: God is great, and to God is praise, God is great, and to God is praise, God The greatest, and praise be to God, there is no god but God alone, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, O God, guide me with guidance, and protect me. With piety, and forgive me in the Hereafter and the First. Then He returns his hand and remains silent as long as a person recites his Fatihah. The book, then he raised his hands again and said something like that, and he continued to do that until he finished. He said: When he saw a strait, he would walk straight up his neck, and when he saw a strait, he would stop, and when he came to one of those mountains, he would stop. At each mountain therein is as much as I say, or the one who says: Her hands stopped but her feet did not stop. He said: Then he descended. His place was on the road, so he set off and I followed him, so I said: Perhaps he will do something from the Sunnah, so he said: I am only going where you know.Then he came and performed ablution on his messengers, then he rode off, and did not pray until a group of people came, so he stood and prayed the sunset prayer, then he turned back to us. He said: The prayer is unified, and he did not separate anything between them. I said: And there was no pause between them except his saying: The prayer is united? Or did he say: A call to prayer except that? He said: No. Then he prayed two rak'ahs for the evening prayer, then he prayed five rak'ahs for the sunset and the evening prayer. He did not volunteer, or he said: He did not perform the prayer. between them with something, then he called for food, and said: Whoever hears our voice, let him come to us. He said: as if he thought that this This is how it should be. Then they spent the night, then he led us in the morning prayer in darkness, and there was not a star in the sky that I recognized but that I saw it, and he recited: (He frowned and turned away) and did not recite Qunoot before or after bowing, then he stood and mentioned some of his supplication in this situation as he did in His position yesterday, then he continued his journey, when he saw a distance, he reached the neck, and when he saw a strait, he caught hold of you. He said: Ibn Abbas told me that the valley in front of him is one of the places called a Muhsir. When he came to him, he ran with his foot, and I knew that he wanted to leave, so I supported him on his camel, so I placed him, and he threw him. The Jamarat, and when the next day he stoned the Jamaraat, he said: I think so. He said to me: With a reward.Then he advanced until he was between them and the middle one, so he mentioned some of his supplication similar to his supplication in the two situations, except that he He added: And be kind to me, or he said: And complete our rites for us. He said: And his standing was as equal to that of any human being, as the reader will see. Surah Yusuf, then he stoned the middle Jamarat, then he went forward and mentioned something like that from his supplication, and like that from his standing."
"14925","(14925) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and he asked about The people came to me, and I said: I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein, so he put his hand to my head, and he took off my button. Then he took off the button of the lower one, then he placed his palm between my breasts. At that time, I was a young boy, and he said: Welcome, O My nephew, ask anything you want? So I asked him while he was blind, and the time for prayer had come, so he stood up in his weaves, wrapped in them. Whenever he placed them on his shoulders, he came back. He turned to her, since she was young, and his cloak was on the side of him on the holder, so he led us in prayer, and I said: Tell me about your Hajj. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: In his hand, so he held nine, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed for nine years without performing Hajj, then he gave the call to prayer. The people on the tenth day: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was performing Hajj. So many people came to Medina, all of them seeking... That he should follow the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and do the same as his work. So we went out with him until we came to Dhul-Halif. Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, and she was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque. How do I do it? He said: Take a bath, and put on a dress.And enter into the ihram, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in the mosque, and he rode the poles until his camel had reached it. On Al-Bayda’, I looked as far as my sight could see, from between his hands, whether riding or walking, and to his right, like that, and from His successor was like that, and those behind him were like that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us and upon him. The Qur’an was revealed, and He knows its interpretation, so whatever He does with it, We do with it, so it is deemed worthy of monotheism: Labbaika. Oh God, O God, O God, O God, You have no partner. O God, indeed, praise, blessings, and dominion are Yours, You have no partner, and the people of The people were insulted by this, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond to any of it, and the Messenger of God remained committed to May God bless him and grant him peace. Jabir said: We only intend to perform Hajj, we do not know the Umrah, even when we come to the House with him, he takes the corner and brakes three times. He walked for four days, then he ran out to the place of Abraham, and recited: {And take the place of Abraham as a place of prayer.} So he made the place between him. And in the middle of the verse, my father used to say: I do not know him to mention it except on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He used to recite In the two rak'ahs: {Say: He is Allah, One} and {Say: O disbelievers},Then he returned to the corner and greeted it, then went out through the door to Al-Safa. When he approached Al-Safa, he recited: {Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God} I begin with what God began with, so he began with As-Safa and proceeded on it until he saw the House, so he faced the House, and God united And He glorified Him and said: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is powerful over all things. There is no god but God alone, He fulfilled His promise, He supported His servant, and He defeated the parties alone, then He called in between that, then He said like that, three times.

 Then he descended to Al-Marwah until his feet reached the bottom of the valley, and when we ascended, he walked until he reached Al-Marwah, and he did so. On Marwa just as he did on Safa, even when it was his last circumambulation of Marwah, he said: If I were to face any matter... I turned around and did not bring the sacrificial animal, and I made it an ‘umrah. So whoever of you does not have a sacrificial animal with you, let him make it permissible and make it an ‘umrah. So Suraq bin Jasham stood up and said: O Messenger of God, is this our year, or is it forever? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, interlocked his fingers, one with the other, and said: The woman has entered into Hajj, twice. No, but forever and ever.Ali came from Yemen with the body of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found Fatima among those who had arrived, and she was wearing bright clothes. She applied kohl, but he denied that to her, so she said: My father ordered me to do this. He said: Then Ali used to say in Iraq: So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urging Fatima for what she had done, seeking a fatwa to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, regarding what she mentioned about him. He said: So I told him that I denied that to her. He said: You are right, you are right. He said: What You said when you made Hajj obligatory? He said: I said: Oh God, I am worthy of declaring what Your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, dedicate to me. He said: If I have a gift, do not permissible. He said: So the group was the guidance that Ali brought from Yemen, and the one that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought. He said: So all of the people dissolved and shortened their prayers, except for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whoever was with him as a guide. When it was the Day of Tarwiyah, they headed to Minna and performed the Hajj, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode and prayed. At noon and afternoon, and sunset, evening, and morning. Then he stayed for a little while until the sun rose, and he ordered that a cloak made of hair be covered. So she struck him with her tiger, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, and the Quraysh did not complain.Except that he was standing at the Sacred Mash'ar, as the Quraysh used to do in the pre-Islamic era, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted it. Peace be upon him, until he came to Arafah and found that his dome had been struck by his tiger, so he descended with it until when the sun had set, he commanded With Al-Qasawi, I departed for him, so he came to the bottom of the valley and addressed the people, and said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you. Like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this polytheism of yours, in this country of yours, except for every matter The pre-Islamic blood is placed under my feet, and the blood of the pre-Islamic period is placed, and the first blood shed from our blood is the blood of Ibn Rabi’ah. Ibn Al-Harith, he was a breastfeeding woman among the Banu Sa’d, and Hudhail killed him. I give up usury, usury of Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, for all of it is subject to usury, so fear Allah regarding women, for you are You took them by the command of God, and you made their private parts permissible with the word of God, and you have a duty to them that no one should settle on your beds. You hate them, but if they do that, beat them severely, and they will give you their provision and clothing. with what is right, and I have left among you what you will never go astray after, if you hold fast to it; The Book of God, and you are being asked about it, so what are you saying? They said: We bear witness that you have conveyed, fulfilled, and been sincere.Then he said: With his index finger, he raised them to the heavens and blessed them with the people: O God, I bear witness, O God, I bear witness, three times. Several times, then he gave the call to prayer, then he stood and prayed the noon prayer, then he stood and prayed the afternoon prayer, and did not pray anything in between. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode until the situation came, then he placed the belly of his she-camel against the rocks, and made He held the rope of the walker between his hands, and he faced the Qiblah, and he did not remain standing until the sun set and the yellow color disappeared a little. Until the disk disappeared, Usama came behind him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pushed the reins, hanging to the runners, until He raised his head to strike your mount, and said with his right hand: O people! Sakina, Sakina, whenever He brought one of the ropes for her and let her relax a little so that she could climb it.

 Until he came to Muzdalifah, he performed the Maghrib and Isha prayers there with one call to prayer and two iqamas, and he did not say any tasbih between them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down until dawn came, and he prayed when dawn became clear to him with the call to prayer and the iqamah, then He rode the qasawi until he came to the Sacred Mash’ar, then he faced the qiblah and called upon Him and glorified Him and swore to Him and to Him alone, and he did not stop. standing until he traveled very far,So he left before the sun rose, and Al-Fadl bin Abbas, who was a beautiful, white-haired, handsome man, came back. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pushed, a group of people passed by running, and Al-Fadl started looking at them, so the Messenger of God sat down. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He placed his hand on his face, and the grace turned his face to the other side to be seen. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned his face to the other side. May God bless him and grant him peace. He turned his hand from the other side to the face of grace, so he turned his face from the other side to look, until he came, giving voice to the Prophet. He moved a little, then took the middle road that leads to the Great Jamarat, until he came to the Jamarat which is at He hit the tree and threw seven pebbles at it, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble, like the pebbles of throwing it. He threw it from the depths of the valley. Then he went to the slaughterhouse and slaughtered sixty-three with his own hand, then he gave Ali and he slaughtered as many as he could, and joined him in it. He guided him, and he commanded everyone to give a portion of it, and it was put in a pot and cooked, so they ate of its flesh and drank of its broth."
"14926","(14926) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: You were commanded in the book to perform four prayers; By performing the prayer, paying the zakat, performing the Hajj, and the Umrah."
"14927","(14927) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about the Sindhi chicken that he took out of the Haram? They said: No, this is hunting."
"14928","(14928) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go around with the men. Ata’ said: And a woman said to Aisha: Come. To the stone and touch it. She said: Depart from yourself."
"14929","(14929) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in the ihram being intimate."
"14930","(14930) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in it."
"14931","(14931) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say about someone who was forced to die and hunt: He eats dead meat, and he does not eat game, nor does it offer it to him, meaning the forbidden."
"14932","(14932) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He recites the Talbiyah on behalf of the mute and the child."
"14933","(14933) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who came for Hajj while she was menstruating, he said: She should perform Hajj for her ‘umrah and proceed to Arafat while performing Hajj."
"14934","(14934) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’; Like him"
"14935","(14935) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Tawoos, he said: I heard him. He was asked about a man who wanted to say the Talbiyah and said “Allahu Akbar”? He said: It is sufficient."
"14936","(14936) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: He will return."
"14937","(14937) Mu’awiyah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, he said: It is sufficient."
"14938","(14938) Abd al-Aziz al-Ammi told us, saying: Matar was asked, and I heard about a woman who asked her husband’s permission to perform Hajj, but he did not. He gave her permission, so she asked for permission to visit, so he gave her permission, so she gathered her white clothes and shouted for Hajj? He said: So they came to Al-Hasan and asked him? Al-Hasan said: Al-Laka’a does not have that. Matar said: And his leaders were asked? He said: She is in a state of ihram. Matar said: So I went to Mecca and asked Al-Hakam bin Utaiba? He said: She is in a state of ihram. Matar said: So I ordered a man to ask Ata bin Abi Rabah? He said: No, not even the blessing of an eye. She does not have that."
"14939","(14939) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Awany told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If it was If she has a mahram, then there is no harm in her going out, and she does not ask for her husband’s permission."
"14940","(14940) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the woman who did not perform Hajj, he said: She should ask her husband’s permission, and if he gives her permission, then that is more beloved to me, but if he does not give her permission, then that is more beloved to me. If she goes out with a mahram, then that is one of the obligations of God Almighty, in which there is no obedience."
"14941","(14941) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Our companions were not They embrace the House."
"14942","(14942) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not embrace the House."
"14943","(14943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; Omar held the stone and kissed it."
"14944","(14944) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I asked Jabir bin Abdullah about a man who performed Umrah and circumambulated the Kaaba, then He wanted to visit his family, before he circumambulated between Safa and Marwa? He said: No, until he circumambulates between Safa and Marwa."
"14945","(14945) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Anas bin Saad; That a man asked Saeed bin Jubayr for a fatwa and said: I performed Hajj with my wife, and I had sexual intercourse with her before I cut my hair short? Saeed said: I will shed blood."
"14946","(14946) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, or Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said: Concerning a woman whose husband had intercourse with her, and the woman had cut her hair, but the man had not cut his hair. He said: There was blood on her."
"14947","(14947) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came A man went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: My sister died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?"
"14948","(14948) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of a man called: Yusuf, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubair; He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my father died and did not perform Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Are you his eldest son? He said: Yes, he said: So he performed Hajj on behalf of your father. Do you think that if your father had a debt, you would have paid it off?

(Nasa’i 3624. Ahmad 4/3)"
"14949","(14949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He performs Hajj on behalf of the dead, even if he has not left a will."
"14950","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abd told us Allah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba Al-Absi said:

(14950) Ibn Fadil narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Duba’a, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me. Peace be upon him, and I am complaining. He said: What do you want? Do you perform Hajj this year? She said: Indeed, I am ill, O Messenger of God. He said: Perform Hajj and say: My place is from the land where You have detained me. (Muslim 104. Ibn Majah 2937)

("
"14951","(14951) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Ali; He used to say: Oh God, perform Hajj if you are able, or Umrah, if you want Umrah, otherwise there is no problem."
"14952","(14952) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Sufyan bin Hussein informed us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon Dubaa’ ibn al-Zubair when she wanted to perform Hajj, and he said to her: Make a condition. When you enter ihram: And my place is wherever you confine me, for that is yours. (Muslim 1068, Ibn Majah 2938)"
"14953","(14953) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: When you perform Hajj, stipulate that: Oh God, I have undertaken the Hajj and I intend to do it, so if Hajj is possible, then it is Hajj, and if I am prevented, then it is Umrah."
"14954","(14954) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: I saw him put his foot in Stitches, then he said: Oh God, I want to perform Hajj if you are able, otherwise, an Umrah if you are able."
"14955","(14955) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Lions used to have their camels led to them, and when they came they would be cowardly. He arrived and wanted to ride, so he said: Oh God, Hajj, if you are able, or else, Omrah, if you are able, then he will perform the Hajj."
"14956","(14956) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: My father did not think there was anything wrong with stipulating Hajj."
"14957","(14957) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Salam, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were not They make conditions, but they do not see the condition as anything. Salam said in his hadith: If only a man were to be tested."
"14958","(14958) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Uthman saw a man standing with his head, and he said to him: You stipulated, he said: Yes."
"14959","(14959) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba On the authority of Uthman and the like."
"14960","(14960) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Subaih, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; In the case of a muhrim, he stipulates, they said: He has a stipulation."
"14961","(14961) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara; Shurayh used to stipulate the Hajj and say: You have known my intention and what I want, so if it is something I should complete, then he would like it. To me, and if it is other than that, then there is no problem. Abu Bakr said: I was informed that Abu Muawiyah retracted this hadith."
"14962","(14962) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The stipulation in Hajj is not With something"
"14963","(14963) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, who said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr: Have you considered the stipulation in Hajj? He said: The stipulation of Hajj is only among people."
"14964","(14964) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; Concerning the condition, they said: It is nothing."
"14965","(14965) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, who said: Alqamah used to stipulate that Hajj was a condition, but he did not think of it as anything."
"14966","(14966) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: The exception. And those who are not excluded are the same."
"14967","(14967) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon his hyenas and said to her: Do you not want to perform the public Hajj? She said: O Messenger of God, I am crippled. He said: Perform Hajj and make conditions. She said: How should I say? He said: Say: Here you are, O God, here you are, my home from the land where You have imprisoned me.

(Abu Dawud 1773. Tirmidhi 941)"
"14968","(14968) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Umairah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If you perform Hajj So he made a condition."
"14969","(14969) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Harith; He used to stipulate the Umrah."
"14970","(14970) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: Concerning a slave who is freed after he sets out. The people left Arafat, or he said: A boy has a wet dream, or a girl has her menstruation, or in combination. So they returned to Arafat and stopped before sunrise. Fajr, the Hajj of Islam is sufficient for them."
"14971","(14971) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who performs Hajj on behalf of another man, and he continues with him. He said: He teaches them, so if they surrender to him, otherwise he turns him away."
"14972","(14972) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad bin Ja’far, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas coming one day Al-Tarwiyah So he kissed the stone, then prostrated on it, and he did that three times."
"14973","(14973) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah; Ibn Abbas prostrated before him."
"14974","(14974) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus; Omar prostrated to him."
"14975","(14975) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abis bin Rabi’ah, who said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab He received the stone and kissed it, and said: Had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissing you, I would not have kissed you.

(Bukhari 1605, Abu Dawud 1868)"
"14976","(14976) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus; Omar kissed the stone three times and prostrated on it for each kiss, and it was mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so."
"14977","(14977) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Issam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjas, who said: I saw the bald man Omar before the stone. He said: I know that you are a stone that does no harm or benefit, and had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissing you, I would not have I kissed you (Ahmad 350 Muslim 250)"
"14978","(14978) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: I saw Omar Ibn Al-Khattab kissed the stone and pressed it close to it, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was very warm to you. 

(Muslim 926. Ahmad 54)"
"14979","(14979) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, he said: I saw a peacock who did it, meaning he prostrated to it."
"14980","(14980) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Between the two mountains of Muzdalifah is The Sacred Mash’ar."
"14981","(14981) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: I did not find anyone to tell me. About the Sacred Mash’ar."
"14982","(14982) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Amr About the Sacred Mash’ar? So I remained silent until the hands of our mounts touched down on Muzdalifah. He said: Where is the one who asked about the Sacred Mash’ar? This is the Sacred Mash’ar."
"14983","(14983) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning his saying: (The Sacred Mash’ar), he said: It is Qazah, and it is all of Muzdalifah."
"14984","(14984) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Looking at the House is an act of worship, and circumambulating the House is a prayer."
"14985","(14985) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Looking at the House is my worship."
"14986","(14986) Waki’ and Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Looking at the House My servants"
"14987","(14987) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Abu Nu’aym al-Nakhi informed me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn al-Aswad, he said: Looking at the House is an act of worship."
"14988","(14988) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They hated for a man wearing shoes to enter the house."
"14989","(14989) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abd Allah bin al-Muzani; Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid said, “In Muharram, there is tea in it.” They said, “There is tea in it.”"
"14990","(14990) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, he said: A man asked Salim and Al-Qasim about some of his accidents. And he is in ihram? One of them said: He should give in charity half a mudd, and the other said: Half a mudd is better than two pieces of water."
"14991","(14991) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mu’amal, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas; Concerning a person in ihram who killed a cat, they said: two thirds of a mud, and two thirds of a mud, I put into the stomach of a poor person from his cat."
"14992","(14992) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Salih Al-Fazari, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid; He was asked about a ihram who killed a cat? He said: He gives in charity a generous amount."
"14993","(14993) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, who said : When she enters the tithe, he must not take any of his hair or his fingernails."
"14994","(14994) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; He said: Whoever wants to make a sacrifice should not take anything from his hair or his nails if he makes a dhali. Hajj"
"14995","(14995) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ahlafi, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He disliked having his hair cut when he wanted to perform Hajj. He said: So I asked Ikrimah? He said: Should he not leave the women?"
"14996","(14996) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked having his hair cut if Hajj was close."
"14997","(14997) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever wants During Hajj, he does not remove any of his hair."
"14998","(14998) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a man who cut some of his hair when he wanted to perform Hajj? He said: There is no harm in it."
"14999","(14999) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Salem, on the authority of Salem; He used to have his head cut off in the middle of Sha`ban, then he would go out and perform Hajj."
"15000","(15,000) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He liked to keep his hair and nails clean during tithe days, and he saw no harm in enlightenment."
"15001","(15001) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Ikrimah, Salim, Ata’, Tawoos, and Al-Qasim? They said: There is no harm in it."
"15002","(15002) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: My mother told me about her grandmother; Indeed, she heard Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, saying: Whoever is offering a sacrifice on his behalf, the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah has come, so no one should take it. Did he feel anything until he sacrificed it? Did I mention that to Abraham? He said: I have not heard of this."
"15003","(15003) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to desire to provide Poetry, if they want to prohibit it."
"15004","(15004) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Hurmuz Al-Araj; Omar bin Al-Khattab took from the head of a man from Quraysh, called: Muhammad bin Abi Rabi’a, he had hair. With the tree before entering ihram."
"15005","(15005) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, Ata bin Yassar, and Abi Bakr bin Sulaiman bin Abi Hatham; They said: There is no harm in a man cutting his hair and nails as part of his tithe."
"15006","(15006) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in enlightenment in the tithe."
"15007","(15007) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr; Jabir bin Zaid was negligent in his tithe."
"15008","(15008) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in enlightenment in the tithe."
"15009","(15009) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab; He used to prefer to keep one’s hair in ihram when entering ihram."
"15010","(15010) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yusuf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, the client of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed his garment by smoothing it while he was in Ihram. (Abu Dawud 1571, Tabarani 11510)"
"15011","(15011) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The person in ihram changes his clothes to whatever he wants, after He wears the clothes of a muhrim."
"15012","(15012) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Sabbah bin Thabit, who said: I asked Sa’id bin Jubayr: Should a person in ihram sell his clothes? He said: Yes."
"15013","(15013) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sabbah, on the authority of Saeed; In the manner of??"
"15014","(15014) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Hajjaj, and Abdul-Malik, And giving; They did not see any harm in a person in ihram changing his clothes, or anything like that."
"15015","(15015) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The person in ihram may change his clothes. Whatever he wants"
"15016","(15016) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He entered the bath of Al-Juhfa while he was in ihram. He said: God will not do anything with your filth."
"15017","(15017) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated for the ihram to enter the bathroom, and he said: He was too busy to enter the bathroom."
"15018","(15018) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; It is disliked for the ihram to enter the bathroom."
"15019","(15019) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Aisha; She saw nothing wrong with a man circumambulating for three or five weeks, and then praying."
"15020","(15020) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; She used to connect the weeks."
"15021","(15021) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: There is no harm in a man doing tawaf for three days. Seven weeks, or five, then he prays two rak'ahs."
"15022","(15022) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; Indeed, it is a bitter horn."
"15023","(15023) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid; He denied it and said: No one did it except a man from Quraysh, Al-Miswar bin Makhramah."
"15024","(15024) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus; He circumambulated for three weeks, then prayed six rak'ahs."
"15025","(15025) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Tawus and Al-Miswar ibn Makhramiya used to marry each other between the weeks, and Ata saw no harm in that."
"15026","(15026) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, he said: I lived in Mecca and then Saeed bin Jubayr and Ali bin Hussein. So Ali bin Hussein went around for three weeks, and prayed two rak’ahs for each week, then he came to the stone and received it, and he was happy. Ibn Jubayr did it during the day."
"15027","(15027) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, who said: They mentioned with Al-Qasim that Aisha used to marry weeks, and he said: Fear God, and do not say about the Mother of the Believers what she did not do."
"15028","(15028) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Years passed that with every Two rak'ahs for a week."
"15029","(15029) Ma’n told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, Salem, and Ubaid Allah bin Abd. To God, they pray two rak'ahs at every week, and they do not connect the seven rak'ahs together."
"15030","(15030) Ma’n narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Kharijiya ibn Zayd praying every week. Two rak'ahs"
